	<body bgcolor="#ffffff" text="#000000">
		<h1 class="largetext">Rodcetnife.org Forums</h1>
		<h2 class="normaltext">General Category => General Discussion => Topic started by: Kinladar on August 29, 2003, 10:33:50 am</h2>

		<table width="90%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
			<tr>
				<td>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kinladar</b> on <b>August 29, 2003, 10:33:50 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Kinda hoping this can be a more civilized discussion than the VN one... my hopes are probably too much, but we'll see.<br /><br />My personal point of view is:<br /><br />1) Ascent<br />2) EiE/DA<br />3) Arirang<br />4) FoT<br />5) Forsaken<br />6) Reign of Swords (One kill from Elementals)<br />7) Union of Power (Killed Emp Ssra)<br />8-9) Hegemony - Menacing Visage<br />10) Not really sure... so many that could fit here, that I'll have to think some more<br /><br />The top 2 are very clear, they're in Plane of Time, so that is easy. Ascent Killed Quarn as well.<br /><br />After that, the lines become a bit more blurred, at least I think they have in the last few months.<br /><br />In the last 3 months, Arirang has been kinda quiet, though it looks like they are working on Xegony, so since they've killed Fennin, that gives them a bit of a leg on FoT on Elemental god progress.<br /><br />FoT has kinda went a bit of a different direction, since Fennin was getting ganked real fast every time they  looked for him, they worked out getting to Xegony Isle, interesting fight, but I can see them beating that one fairly soon I think. Right now, I think they could do Fennin once we catch him. <br /><br />Forsaken has made some astounding progress, and much as it may pain anyone to admit, they will probably continue to progress, but at what rate has yet to be seen. There are rumors of some encounters getting gimped, namely Rallos Zek (again). I think SoE has changed the Rallos Zek encounter so many times, it's crazy.<br /><br />So again, top 2 are simple answers, beyond that... well, there's only a fine line between Arirang and FoT atm, with Forsaken getting a streak of kills the last few weeks. <br /><br />I think Forsaken will have to turn Farm mode on much as Arirang and FoT have to be able to attempt the Elemental gods. That takes time with the lower number of drops in Elementals compared to a place like VT, and the stiff competition with 2 other guilds already there.<br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>EQSysquella</b> on <b>August 30, 2003, 01:15:45 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">4) Hamsters of War<br />5) Fires of TIme<br />etc etc<br /><br />ya forgot that</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kelce</b> on <b>August 31, 2003, 11:09:44 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">The usual Kinladar, however, Hege's killed Bertox, Terris, Behemoth and AoW. I'd say they're clearly #9.<br /><br />Missing:<br />- Seeker's of Dawn/Ugou No Sayo<br />- Dragon's Fist<br />- Spirit of Verzi<br />- Century of Flame</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Turboo</b> on <b>August 31, 2003, 02:04:43 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Not that im eager to place Verzi high in ranking, but using Emp/VT to measure with is kinda outdated i think, cause for instance i dont belive Verzi aiming to ever go there . I dont know if any other guild out there thinking of passing on Emp n VT.<br />But i for one belive that u can advance without going there, since the introduction of Ornate armor etc etc, Clerics can get max FT  and decent resists without going to VT without any problems, aswell as the rest of the casters.<br /><br /> </div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kinladar</b> on <b>August 31, 2003, 07:17:00 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">That was kinda what I didn't know. If someone can kinda give a list of what each of those guild have had in regards to biggest kill... etc... fills in the blanks somewhat.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>EQSysquella</b> on <b>September 02, 2003, 11:42:36 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">you can advance without emp/vex.. RoS has proven that.. Im sure any guild can do it, but I love Vex<br /><br />=)</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kinladar</b> on <b>September 03, 2003, 08:38:36 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">You can advance without Emp, but it's still an impressive accomplishment, and I think it will benefit UoP alot once they get the feel, and strategies down pat for VT.<br /><br />Not as many places one can go and get as many loot drops that are serious upgrades for so many in a single clearing. <br /><br />Add in the time needed to accomplish keying thier guild and I think it shows a huge amount of discipline. You will note that I did position RoS above UoP, because they have gone the non-VT route, and succeeded. Now even some of thier members are Elemental Flagged. I am quite sure they will kill RZTW on thier own soon enough, and fill in the gaps in guild flags.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kelce</b> on <b>September 03, 2003, 11:42:16 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">1) Ascent<br />2) EiE/DA<br />3) Arirang<br />4) FoT<br />5) Forsaken<br />6) Reign of Swords<br />7) Union of Power<br />8.) Hegemony<br />9) Spirit of Verzi<br />11) Century of Flame, Apotheosis, Menacing Visage<br />12) Dragon's Fist, Outcast Adventurers<br />13) Brew Masters<br />14) Exiled Knights<br />15) Tul Acharn? GC? AK?I have no idea below this.<br /></div>
					<br />
