					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">1) Ascent<br />2) EiE/DA<br />3) Arirang<br />4) FoT<br />5) Forsaken<br />6) Reign of Swords<br />7) Union of Power<br />8.) Hegemony<br />9) Spirit of Verzi<br />10) Century of Flame, Apotheosis, Menacing Visage<br />11) Dragon's Fist, Outcast Adventurers<br />12) Brew Masters<br />13) Exiled Knights<br />14) Tul Acharn? GC? AK? <b>Adventurers Company (AC)</b>  (shameless plug) heh I have no idea below this.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Strumph Phyton</b> on <b>September 05, 2003, 06:43:38 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I'd like to point out that YES our guild leader can't even count to 10, but he has been getting tutored  ;D</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kinladar</b> on <b>September 11, 2003, 11:14:14 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">1) Ascent<br />2) EiE/DA<br />3) Arirang<br />4) FoT<br />5) Reign of Swords (Full Elemental Flagged with less)<br />6) Forsaken<br />7) Union of Power<br />8.) Hegemony<br />9) Spirit of Verzi<br />10) Century of Flame, Apotheosis, Menacing Visage<br />11) Dragon's Fist, Outcast Adventurers<br />12) Brew Masters<br />13) Exiled Knights<br />14) Tul Acharn? GC? AK? Adventurers Company <br /><br />Ok, my reason for moving Reign of Swords over Forsaken, they are accomplishing with deft skills what Forsaken needs blunt numbers to acheive. Riegn of Swords is doing the same targets that FoT has been with the same numbers, (IE FoT only needs 50-60 to do Rallos Zek, 45 or so for Solusek Ro.) on a more casual basis.<br /><br />From that standpoint, Killing Emp means nothing. Any guild that can defeat Rallos on thier own, can certainly do the Emp. <br /><br />Another thing to consider, there are now 4 guilds Elemental Farming.<br /><br />One that's PoEB flagged, has killed Fennin Ro, and has Xegony Isle Key.<br /><br />One that Has Killed Fennin Ro, and Has Xegony Isle Key.<br /><br />2 That are fairly new to Elementals and I'm sure working towards similar goals as the first two.<br /><br />What I'm driving at is that the spaces between spots 3-6 are very small, and could be leap frogged pretty fast if certain chains of events occur. But despite what some on other boards are saying, none of these guilds are &quot;stagnant and dying.&quot;  If anything, they are all progressing, and moving forward at good rates.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kelce</b> on <b>September 15, 2003, 09:19:35 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Is RoS VT keyed?<br /><br />If not I'd still keep them just under Forsaken, for the moment, since Forsaken can very quickly gear new applicants, alts and bots there. Especially casters.<br /><br />VT being the candystore it is they can backfarm it.<br /><br />RoS, without VT access has to scour PoP for similar quality drops.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Heloisa</b> on <b>September 15, 2003, 11:37:19 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Hiya guys.<br /><br />RoS is getting closer to becoming  VT keyed as most members have 80% of their shards done.   <br /><br />More importanly (obviously), within the next month or so we should have most folks (90%+ of the guild) emp key enabled.  This will at least put us in a reasonable postion to finally take a shot at the Emp.<br /><br />From a personal stand point,  VT is my &quot;end game&quot; and can't wait to set foot in there!! :bounce<br /><br />I just need the rift /sniff  oh and that pesky insignia  :)<br /><br />cheers</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Turboo</b> on <b>September 16, 2003, 03:44:34 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">As a true verzi member i think i would like to move verzi up a tad bit, i think we past Hegemony ..and UoP i dont know about but if not past, we next aside to em =)<br /><br />Could be me dreaming tho..i often do ...=)</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kinladar</b> on <b>September 16, 2003, 09:17:13 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I primarily consider RoS a better guild because of progression in the current raiding expansion, and not the previous one.<br /><br />Luclin, then PoP equal raiding expansions, Ykesha, and LDoN are not what I would say follows the thoughts of raiding expansions, so don't really count a great deal towards the total. This is of course my personal opinion, and feel free to tell me I'm full of it  ;D<br /><br />RoS deserves more credit because they've been able to accomplish far more than anyone probably thought they could. They zipped through alot of content pretty quick in PoP once they focused on it. Now that they have gained alot of nice upgrades in PoP, them getting VT access is simply a matter of getting the members all keyed, and downing the Emp. If they can take Rallos Zek, they can take Emp. I just personally consider RoS a more skilled guild is all. Anyone can post thier own revisions though.<br /><br />The only thing that throws me off, is what Verzi, and others like Seekers of Dawn do on a semi regular basis. Not sure of either's overall progression etc...</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kelce</b> on <b>September 17, 2003, 10:05:30 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Heloisa $txt[176] September 15, 2003, 11:37:19 am</div><div class="quote">RoS is getting closer to becoming  VT keyed as most members have 80% of their shards done.   <br /><br />More importanly (obviously), within the next month or so we should have most folks (90%+ of the guild) emp key enabled.  This will at least put us in a reasonable postion to finally take a shot at the Emp.<br /><br />I just need the rift /sniff  oh and that pesky insignia  :)<br /></div><br /><br /> ;D<br /><br />I'm a big fan of RoS, having RL friends in there. *big cheers Heloisa* I got my insignia last month, just waiting to get the pouches..<br /><br />I suppose Kin and I will have to agree that we disagree, heh. Forsaken will continue to enjoy success in the Elemental Planes, while RoS will spend some time in VT.<br /><br />Between Hegemony and Spirit of Verzi, I would feel that Hegemony is ahead, however, since they've down Tallon Zek, Vallon?. SoV's recent Behemoth kill was nice to see. Gratz on that btw SoV!</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Gabus</b> on <b>September 17, 2003, 10:14:15 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Kinladar $txt[176] September 16, 2003, 09:17:13 am</div><div class="quote">. This is of course my personal opinion, and feel free to tell me I'm full of it  ;D<br /><br />RoS deserves more credit because they've been able to accomplish far more than anyone probably thought they could. They zipped through alot of content pretty quick in PoP once they focused on it. Now that they have gained alot of nice upgrades in PoP, them getting VT access is simply a matter of getting the members all keyed, and downing the Emp. If they can take Rallos Zek, they can take Emp. I just personally consider RoS a more skilled guild is all. Anyone can post thier own revisions though.<br /><br /></div><br /><br />Kin, you are full of it :P   hehe couldnt resist.<br /><br />Anyways, I would tend to weight the actuall action over the speed at which it was attained, which is the primary reason for your placement of RoS. Life in EQ is much easier now for any guild. Gear is better and cheaper, there has been incredible implosion of the mid range guilds, resulting in a freeing up of talent, that untill recently (started in the spring of this year) was unavailable. Additionally, there is a bigger pool of 65's to draw from. Encounters are mapped, simplified, and revealed already on sites. Simply put it is easier now than it has been for previous guilds.<br /><br />This is not to sell short what RoS has done. They HAVE progressed at an incredible rate, and do appear to be VERY skilled and focused. My caution is moving them up because of their speed, rather than purely what they have accomplished. If you do that, then you are going to have to go back and look at the difficulty many other guilds had comming up.<br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kinladar</b> on <b>September 17, 2003, 01:03:43 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Forsaken and RoS are both very recently Elemental Flagged. Both I would assume had access to similar information.<br /><br />RoS has fewer members overall than Forsaken does to use in encounters on an average basis. At least from general guild roster size anyhow. They are now learning the elemental planes, and what they have to offer. The only thing that VT would give them that Elementals does not, is the speed of upgrades in a single night. VT can drop a large number of upgrades in a clearing, but it's a 7 day spawn. Elementals are a shorter spawn, but there's a ton of competition. Those two facts by themselves will slow both Forsaken and RoS down a bit in Elementals, since you have 4 other guilds already raiding there. Some more than others of course.<br /><br />And of course I'm full of it Gabus, I gotta take the WS all the time to make the Paladins look good  :chair</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
