					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>maxo</b> on <b>December 04, 2003, 09:53:04 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I&#039;m flattered by our placement considering we only have 7-9 raiding hours a week and voluntary-not required at that.<br /><br />Our clock is very different than the uber clock.  When I read someone&#039;s post that they are casual and raid 4-5 days a week I&#039;m amazed.<br /><br />You guys who work so hard at the game have earned your place as the top guilds.<br /><br />Being gamers since way back- we do place a premium on skill and we have some significant challenges and benefits.<br /><br />Often, by the time we get to a scenario, we are a bit over-leveled for it.  It would be nice to hit it at the &quot;right&quot; level but it has to be up for us to kill it and that is rare.<br /><br />Often, by the time we get to a scenario another expansion has come out and made the content easier. <br /><br />on the other hand.<br />Often, by the time we get to content, the drop rate is usually nerfed all to hell so it takes us 3 times as long to gear up.<br /><br />Often the encounter has been made a lot tougher than it was for the top two guilds.  We are not going to be able to use four enchanters to beat behemoth while the rest of the guild waits near by to get their flag.  That got nerfed. <br /><br />Some guilds say they are a &quot;family&quot; guild, I&#039;d call the Brews more of a &quot;corporate&quot; guild at this point.  The requirements of PoP means we have to blow up like a puffer fish to do some of the encounters.  I would have preferred that we could have stayed about 50 members with 36 on raid nights.  <br /><br />If I was going to venture at ALL into negative territory it would be this.  I do not think much of guilds built by people who were equipped by other guilds and then left them.  I&#039;m not including folks who were caught in guilds that just crumbled.<br /><br /> I&#039;m talking about the folks who get guilds to equip them and then do not pay back that effort.  It is part of what forced us to a point system.  It was pretty disgusting to stay up late on a work night to help someone and then 2 weeks later they say, &quot;sorry, I&#039;m going to leave to see the highest parts of the game.&quot;<br />I have little respect for these people.<br /><br />On the other hand, the folks who pay back their guild with a couple months of helping others or even better help before hand and who simply play more than we do I understand.   We have a small crowd of Brew alumni who have moved on to guilds there in the top 10 who I&#039;m very happy for and still happy to hang out from time to time.<br /><br />It was said in another post that we are full of ourselves by that statesman of the server, foulwind.  Well I guess we are very proud of our guild.  It won&#039;t be the top 10 guilds- but it has a fair shot at being elemental when we have played the same number of hours as you guys have.<br /><br />And we will have done it mostly from scratch from the first days of June 1999 when we would wait til 10pm cst for Gravelox to log on so we would have a cleric and we could do something.<br /><br />I want to take a moment to mourn the Alliance.  If it had not had it&#039;s political, level split and casual vs uber-casual issues, it had a shot at being truly uber on a voluntary basis.  The road with Ghost Chapel, Adventurers Company, Aurora Knights, and Trouble&#039;s Band was a nice one to share. <br /><br />Oh and Brews finally have an enraging weapon.  Woo hoo!  That&#039;s going to help a lot.<br /><br />Anyway grats to all you guys on the leader board.  That represents a lot of hard work and skillful play.<br /><br /></div>
					<br />
