					Post by: <b>Chroam</b> on <b>December 11, 2003, 03:15:32 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Hegemony has 4 kills in VT (all four being that monster of all fights, Thall Va Xakra); thus 16 VT loots.<br /><br />One or two people with VT gear from other sources, not much.<br /><br />Hegemony doesn&#039;t have Plane of Fire access in general, though, again, a few people do.<br /><br />I rank the top guild as follows:<br /><br />1) Ascent<br />2) tie - Dol/EiE<br />4) FoT<br />5) Forsaken<br />6) Arirang<br />7) Conviction<br />8) Hegemony<br />9) UoP<br />10) RoS<br /><br />Ascent first by being insane.  ;)<br /><br />Dol Amroth and Echos in Eternity#2 (tied, because they *are* seperate guilds).<br /><br />Fires of Time ahead of Forsaken based on my personal opinion of who will be in Time first.<br /><br />Conviction ahead of Hegemony based on Elemental status (i.e. PoF).<br /><br />Hegemony ahead of Union of Power based on Elemental status.<br /><br />Union of Power ahead of Reign of Swords because (I&#039;ve been told) of recent problems RoS had with Emp (not just once, nor even twice); real questions in my mind about their abilities after the split.<br /><br />I&#039;m thinking that Arirang is really stagnating.  Forsaken and FoT have both basically passed them by.<br /><br />What has Conviction done in Elementals?  &lt;- serious question, I don&#039;t know.<br /><br /><br />later,<br />Chroam<br />--of Hegemony</div>
