					Post by: <b>Jeet</b> on <b>December 14, 2003, 05:42:04 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">&quot;Pre-Elemental stuff is in no way equal to AHR loot. I may be wrong,  there might be one or 2 slots that are close but I doubt it.&quot;<br /><br />Oh really.<br /><br />I was specifically referring to the BP/Legs on AHR (slots that are never easy to upgrade), as well as the quest neck.  Everything else absolutely can be matched by things dropped pre-elemental, particularly off the mobs Ssnakess mentioned.<br /><br />Where you are really going to lose this argument is weapons when comparing pre-elemental vs. VT.   Pretty obvious since VT has a total of 0 weapons (at least anything you would use outside of VT).    And while not a smorgasborg, you do get weapon selection pre-elemental, but probably the most bang for your buck  would be the Blade of War.<br /><br />Let me throw a question at you.  You can only choose one of these:  Your top cleric with an AHR bp, or your top warrior with a Blade of War.  Which would you choose?  I can already tell you 10 out of 10 times which one will make your raiding more efficient (and will probably be using until you find a time-level equivalent).<br /><br /><br /></div>
