					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>A Mammal</b> on <b>December 15, 2003, 01:54:15 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Technically you didn&#039;t have to have Beastlords to advance to the next lvl in Luclin. I&#039;m pretty sure the new class crap will just be eye candy for people that play just to lvl characters to 25 and never really do anything in the game. <br /><br />The new lvls if there actually put in will just slow guilds down by a few weeks. Most likely what they will do is a mixure of flags + keys. Flag for a certain zone then the whole guild has to do a mini VT key type quest. <br /><br />Thats really the only way this next expansion won&#039;t be beat within the first 2 months of its going live. From the rumors you hear, and them wanting to milk at least 2 expansions out of EQ before it dies; I would think they would put in flag + very hard whole guild key quest.<br /><br />Hope they don&#039;t go that way and just create an ass load of content, but this is SOE and we all know thats not going to happen. If they put in new lvls to 70 or 75 it will cripple old content to the point every casual player and there next door neighbor will have Elemental access at least. <br /><br />Which brings me back to my orginal point as to why I&#039;m so interested in what the next expansion truely holds.  </div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Eelyen</b> on <b>December 15, 2003, 02:12:34 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I suspect 1 or 2 high end situations occurring.<br /><br />1) They add Instancing for all new high end content, allowing each guild to do their own thing.  Thus, letting people finish off their days of everquest without issues.<br /><br />2) Added Major Cockblocking encounters back into the mix which helps seperate the guilds again.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Vosh</b> on <b>December 15, 2003, 02:42:01 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">EQ&#039;s always been a game of math, and as our understanding of the system increased since release we can reflect on how expansions proportionaly (or not) increased the scale of numbers we were working with.<br /><br />Each expansion dating its predecessors based on what was considered reasonable proportion at the time. Exceptions of course like LoY, where aside from armour dyes was a miserable failure IMO in the attempt to promote that side of the world. <br /><br />The two most significant recently being Luclin, Pop, and in terms of gear augmentation LDoN. Ssra, VT and perhpas the plains for lower levels are still popular with some guilds and provide adequate loot though not for the amount of time required. <br /><br />Pop introduced a bold new concepts like  &quot;planer progression&quot; which came as an extension of the thinking behind keying for VT but on a broader scale and didn&#039;t have the flaw of confining hateful masses of people in one zone trying to beat each other to key parts (refering primarily to Ssra keys).<br /><br />Frustrating in its own way though as any Elemental guild can atest to the wretched bitch that is &quot;reflagging&quot;. Which I believe has led to some as before unheard of cooperation inter-guild for flagging newcomers. This is all well and good but the content of Pop invoked the last of the pattern SOE had been following in opening &quot;Planar&quot; zones and offering up a random god as an end boss. Fear, Hate, Mischief (soft of), and then most of the significant gods put on a plate for our gaming consumption. <br /><br />Those who are fortunate enough to reach the paragon of this have have in their possession or access to unbelieveable gear pushing ridiculous numbers. Gear from Time followed not too terribly far by Elemental gear is of a factor greater then we have seen before. <br />Adding to this LDoN where this gear can be augmented to an even higher insanity where do you go from there?<br /><br />Cthulian horrors? A mythos expansion of current themes which at this point could be kind of dull. Whatever they design they have already made their statistical bed, now I&#039;m just curious as to what level ranges they plan to be sleeping in it with.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Ssnakess</b> on <b>December 15, 2003, 06:18:19 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: A Mammal $txt[176] December 15, 2003, 01:33:21 pm</div><div class="quote">Which means there will be a rather large chunk of the server in Elemental and Time gear by the time the next expansion comes out. <br /><br />Unless the next expansion is filled with mobs harder then mobs in time most of this server will rip threw the content faster then any other expansion so far. <br /><br />When you look at top ten list, and pretty much all 10 are in Elementals or Time, its something we have never seen, and I&#039;m interested what effect it will have on the game. When we started PoP there weren&#039;t ten guilds in VT. <br /></div><br /><br />I&#039;d have to disagree.  The thing about Time is, while it is instanced for several guilds, you cannot have more than one guild in timeb at once.  Meaning that whenever a guild enters, they will have fewer and fewer days to learn the encounters which is of course based on how many guilds are ahead of them, and how long it takes them to clear.<br /><br />For example.  Currently, I believe it takes EiE/DA 2-3 days to clear time (lets say 3).  It takes us 1 day.  That means when FoT gets to potime, they will have 3 days to learn the encounters, barring of course that they can outmobilize one of us on one of the days we plan to do time.<br /><br />Now, if it takes a guild getting 6-7 days to try potime per week) a few months to learn, then it would theoretically take twice that amount of time for a guild only getting 3 days a week. <br /><br />This of course means that Forsaken, who will likely be in potime within the next 3 months, will arrive while FoT is probably just hitting phase 4.  Meaning they will get pretty much one chance a week to learn potime, maybe more if they are willing to start outrageously early to learn.  And if perhaps we have moved on by then they could get an extra day, or FoT could.  By that time I would imagine EiE/DA is down to a one day clear (max of 2), but with FoT still progressing through the encounters than Forsaken&#039;s time would be rather limited.<br /><br />So basically to sum it up, every guild that enters potime cuts the amount of time (I love the word time, its so great using it multiple times per sentence..) the next guild in line has to learn each encounter.  Lengthening how long it takes them to learn the content, and thus keeping guilds spread apart.<br /><br />I really don&#039;t see a clumping of fully geared guilds before the next expansion.  While EiE/DA will be geared with lots of potime gear, we will have more.  And the same can be said for every guild that gets there.  We will have more than EiE/DA, they will have more than FoT, who will have more than Forsaken, and so on.<br /><br />Grats me on rambling.  I win at EQ.  If you read all that, I am rather surprised, and I would like to offer you a cookie.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kweil</b> on <b>December 15, 2003, 08:13:26 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I read it, can I get my cookie now?</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>A Mammal</b> on <b>December 15, 2003, 08:32:05 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">While its true that Time has a funnel affect I think your missin the point as to what I was saying. Lots of guilds in Elementals makes for alot of people with alot of good gear on. Even the mighty Ssnakess is still wearin Elemental gear. I mean alot of Ascent members which have been in Time for lots of time will still have Elemental pieces on. <br /><br />Which brings me to my point.. <br />All these people with Elemental gear and lets say 30% of this pool (of people) with Time gear are going to own a expansion that doesn&#039;t at least present time quality challanges. <br /><br />To give you a example:<br />Say Forsaken, FoT, Conviction, RoS, Hegemony, and Arirang Farm elementals for the next 2 and 1/2 months. The majority of their members are going to have quite a few Elemental pieces. If you step back and look at Luclin to PoP you see something totally different. About 3 guilds or less that had a few members in VT gear on adverage per server. I mean you get alot of gear in the system cause of 3 day spawns compared to 7 day spawns. <br /><br />Point being that while we step into the &quot;Black Hole&quot; of the next expasion you will see about 8 to 10 guilds that are even in gear going after the same targets. Aside from Ascent and Dol/EiE that will have just a fair percentage advantage from Time gear. More and more guilds will step into Time as well, as time marches on, which will give them the same advantage.<br /><br />Like Eelyen said about them Instancing mobs, which I think they will do, it kinda kills the game from competition. A game without competition turns into masterbation. <br /><br />If I&#039;ve said it once I&#039;ve said it three times already.. I&#039;m very interested to see what they do to keep competition in the game while making a worthwhile expansion. <br /><br />Yes, I know this is step off away from the cock measuring fest of the top ten guild list, but I would like to hear what people think about the next expansion and what we will have to see in order to make it worthwhile. <br /><br />Ssnakess.. wheres my cookie..</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Dravack</b> on <b>December 15, 2003, 10:01:25 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">Pop introduced a bold new concepts like  &quot;planer progression&quot; which came as an extension of the thinking behind keying for VT but on a broader scale and didn&#039;t have the flaw of confining hateful masses of people in one zone trying to beat each other to key parts (refering primarily to Ssra keys).<br /></div><br /><br />VT key was by no means a new idea by SoE.  Velious had ST keys for one.  And I still cringe just thinking about doing my old VP key in Kunark.<br /><br />If you are talking progression to VT by the fact you had to kill emp, that is still similair to the old VP key, it requires a Trak kill (hardest mob mob outside of VP then.)</div>
