					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Delheru</b> on <b>December 19, 2003, 01:31:14 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Adjustments to Glaydes list.<br /><br />Original Game was pretty much owned by AoD/AL. They killed pretty much everything until EL broke the monopoly with Innoruuk (HoS/EL had killed one CT in a pretty massive gimpathon before tho!). Anyway:<br /><br />AoD/AL                - 10 all first, superior farming<br />EL                      - 6 second with gods, early dragons<br />HoS                    - 5 real early Vox, skillz with dragons<br />DA                     - 4 was born pretty late, but early Nags<br />EK                     - 1 farm galore, late Nags<br />AD                    - 1 later Nags<br /><br /><br /><br />Kunark:<br />AoD/AL/EL          - 10 ran through with mass. First outdoor<br />                          dragons and FAs. Little skill.<br />HoS                  - 8 Pimp skill. First VS.<br />AD                    - 9 First Traks.<br />EK                    - 7 rivaled the zerg alliance for a while.       <br />                          Failed.<br />DA/EiE               - 3 Trailed behind. Loss of Vyel set them<br />                          back a bit I think.<br />CoS/MM             - 2 Spirited PoAir clear.<br /><br /><br />Velious:<br />Ascent              - 10. Overthrew AoD/AL/EL during this.<br />AoD/AL             - 9 Still actually rivaling<br />EK/Arirang         - 5 CoV faction and timezone kept them<br />                         alive through the intense spawnhogging<br />                         caused by the AoD/AL vs Ascent rivalry.<br />DA/EiE              - 2 They didn&#039;t survive as well.<br />DF                   - 1 even worse<br /><br /><br />Luclin:<br />Ascent              - 10 pretty much all firsts except glyphed<br />                          and exiled.<br />AoD/AL             - 6 trailing way behind and imploding<br />DA/EiE              - 4 came up to fill the vacuum, but frankly<br />                         only got the mobs they were given<br />Arirang             - 4 timezone advantage proving insufficient<br />                         to get Emperor. F cursed farmers tho.<br />WoW/DF           - 1. Hard to call them progressers in luclin<br />                         when they did only velious stuff during<br />                         luclin<br /><br /><br />PoP:<br />Ascent            - 10 Every first there was to kill.<br />DA/EiE             - 6 trailing just as much as before, but more<br />                        a way more clear #2 of the non-asians<br />Arirang            - 6 probably Arirangs finest hour, since this<br />                       time their success had nothing to do with<br />                       timezone<br />FoTime           - 2 up and coming, but leaking skill to Ascent<br />Forsaken         - 2 always been somewhere back there, but<br />                       finally entering radar range.<br /><br /><br />Current:<br />Ascent           - 10 There&#039;s no real challenge even now<br />DA/EiE            - 8 ascent had nowhere to go, and a lot of<br />                       key people did not like LDoN, so catching up<br />                       has happened<br />Fires of Time   - 6 moving on up in what seems more potent<br />                      than Forsakens climb<br />Forsaken        - 5 there keeping FoTime company<br />Conviction      - 4 I know some of these people are badass,<br />                      and might even be a danger for FoT and<br />                      certainly Forsaken if they chose to compete<br />Arirang           - 2 wru?</div>
