					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Jeet</b> on <b>December 23, 2003, 09:51:55 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"> &quot;oh and for your info there jeet im swinging a bloodfrenzy and a bonechiller and with the anger 3 augments and with the openings crap doesnt really matter if i have a bow if i have both weaps augmented with anger 3 ( not that i would pass a bow over ) &quot;<br /><br />You are gona cry bloody murder when you start taking ripostes from the real DPS dealers in PoP until you get some decked out HP/AA.<br /><br />&quot;but vt is the best way to go and the guilds that take the time and spend a month or two in vt are gonna get the guild on avg tanks over 8k there casters to ft 15 and there casters with over 5k in mana faster then any pre ele. mob will ever do.&quot;<br /><br />You are one of the people I was referring to when I said don&#039;t waste my 2 hours of work.  Take a real good look at Tier 2/3 HP/Mana numbers.<br /><br />And if you need an excessive amount of FT pre-elemental you are doing something wrong.<br /><br />Let me put it this way.  Guild A and Guild B have equal knowledge of pre-elemental zones, and have just killed emp but are Luclin geared.  Guild A decides to farm VT for 2 months.  Guild B decides to go straight into PoP.  <br /><br />Guild A is going to get left in Guild B&#039;s dust.  That is a 100% gaurantee.<br /><br />I&#039;ll spell it out for you.  Your utopian plan of spreading gear into your whole guild while noble, is simply not efficient progression wise.<br /><br />A core group of players is all you need to keep top-end geared for you to functionally progress thru most if not all of the game.   I know this is a hard to swallow fact for alot of people, but it&#039;s a fact none the less.<br /><br />Gear will trickle down to everyone in your guild naturally as you progress further.  If you try to stall yourself with the intent to gear everyone in your guild, it&#039;s simply inefficient in the grand progression scheme.<br /><br />But that&#039;s just my opinion.<br /><br />And no I&#039;m not being an &quot;elitist&quot;.  I&#039;m simply rebutting your &quot;the VT guild will speed by those that didnt&quot; statement, because it&#039;s 110% false.    Maybe you should actually do PoP targets first before you knock the gear.  Hell try looking up gear on the net for that matter.<br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Bowslinger</b> on <b>December 23, 2003, 10:40:35 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I would have to agree w/ Jeet. I have always stated that gearing up everyone was a waste of time and not needed. But how can you explain to 80 people that they don&#039;t get any loot until the core is geared up. They don&#039;t like to hear that and will leave your guild in a heartbeat.<br /><br />You say to spend 2 months in VT, but for some folks it takes 6 months just to get ready to get keyed. Most folks just don&#039;t have the insane amount of patience to do that. I for one quit over VT. After over 300 hours of grinding I still had not one part of a SSRA ring to show for my effort and didn&#039;t intend on spending one more minute trying to get one.<br /><br />So it&#039;s a toss up I guess. You can do VT and destroy your mind or destroy your mind doing POP w/ no VT gear. I would say the time spent will end up the same. Either way, your mind will be destoyed.</div>
					<br />
