					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kinladar</b> on <b>January 06, 2004, 03:59:07 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Not sure the server is shrinking so much, as mud-flation is taking effect in more ways now.<br /><br />People see PoP level gear, and that it&#039;s easier to get and so much better than Velious, and Luclin gear, so they are bypassing it for PoP.<br /><br />I know many people who go that route, and are not even giving older expansions a second thought. <br /><br />This is not new to the game though. You had similar thngs going on with Veeshan&#039;s Peak, when people were working on Luclin, and Velius Targets, Kunark Targets tended to be forgotten more. Now they are not even thought about. Much the same with Velious.<br /><br />Might also speak to an aging of the Everquest player base, and that Everquest itself is changing to reflect that. Many more people are growing up, have families, kids now, but still want to play. Hence the advent of LDoN, where you can slowly aquire gear, and upgrades, on more of your own schedule, versus huge raiding systems.<br /><br />Might be a combination of all this, but who knows.<br /><br />And Grem, you&#039;re going to go blind.</div>
					<br />
