					Post by: <b>Serepi</b> on <b>January 12, 2004, 02:31:46 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Both Bert and Saryrn are &quot;pull out your hair&quot; mindnumbingly dull encounters.  I think Heg must do Bert differently than what I&#039;m seeing posted; we don&#039;t run from spawns to spawn, we just pull everything into the summoners room as it comes.  Granted, it&#039;s non-stop fighting, but for a shaman, it&#039;s utterly boring.  Add that on to Bert being immune to slow and the whole encounter just flat out stinks for the thumb-twiddling shaman.  The trash die too fast to make slows effective and you can&#039;t get Bert. <br /><br />Not that Saryrn&#039;s any better...And the annoying mini&#039;s on the way.  Not difficult, just annoying.  The only saving grace is that Saryrn is quite easy to drop, and she&#039;s fun to look at before you engage!</div>
					<br />
