					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>maxo</b> on <b>March 17, 2004, 01:15:27 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">What can you say about a guild like Township Rebellion... the best guild money can buy.<br /><br />It would be like having a baseball league and letting one team spend 70 million on salary and equipment while another team has about 4 million.<br /><br />Oh wait, they do that and call it a fair competition too.<br /><br />----<br /><br />If you want a semi-&quot;fair&quot; competition- then set up a server that limits all of us to 12 hours a week play time.  Now the fact that someone who is a no-life loser without a job living on their parents money or dealing drugs (uber guild member in the news last year) so they can play 100+ hours a week doesn&#039;t skew the results.  Instead, with a realistic time limit that applies to all your competitors, your progress becomes an issue of logistical, tactical, and other skills.  <br /><br />Of course that still doesn&#039;t address the fact that since the game started, folks who can log on before 4pm EST own the game.    Wow- what skill- you can log on before me.  I&#039;m terribly impressed at your leet early log on skills.<br /><br />At least I got them to randomize the spawn times at the Dallas fan faire.  Prior to that most the mobs were dead before I even got home from work since they all spawned at server reset and stood like ducks in a shooting gallery for the daytime uber guild to race around killing all of them.  When I talked to the Verant folks they had never really considered that for some unknown reason.<br /><br />Since the game is inherently unbalanced as giving the folks who log on early three queens in chess, I don&#039;t see how anyone can take pride in their accomplishments relative to other people.  So that leaves competing against the game- not others.<br /><br />Hell, for all we know, the Brewmasters may have finished the same content in a lot less hours than it took you to finish it (and probably did given that we have equipment and abilities that you did not have access to).  So if we did it in 10 hours a piece and it took you 50 hours a piece then who is the more skillful?  Or does having the equipment make us less skillful.   <br /><br />And who really cares?  We are not talking rocket science (as a gamer for 29 years this game is mechanically trivial compared to say &quot;star fleet battles&quot; (6+ binders of rules) or &quot;D-Day&quot;)  (5000+ counters and a thick rule book) or anything that requires more than just boatloads of time to beat.  <br /><br />Oooooo.  You are more skillful at playing more hours a week than I am and logging on before I log on so you get the camps.  <br /><br />---<br /><br />Anyway- thanks to those who gratz&#039;d Simplee&#039;s post- I&#039;ve met her in RL and she&#039;s a nice person.  To the rest, well your in company with Desert Rat aka Foulwind and if that makes you happy more power to you.<br /></div>
