					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I think people derive satisfaction from the misery of others because they can sit back and think to themselves, &quot;Gee, I know I suck, but at least I don&#039;t suck *as bad as* those guys.&quot;  It&#039;s a pride thing.<br /><br />It&#039;s the same reason the Jerry Springer show was popular.  You can watch it and it&#039;s very reassuring:  &quot;My life may be bad, but at least I&#039;m not sleeping with the sister of my baby&#039;s daddy, who&#039;s a prostitute, and 16 years old to boot!&quot;<br /><br />I said it before, and I&#039;ll say it again:  Schadenfreude.  It&#039;s what makes the EQ world go round.</div>
