					Post by: <b>Kinladar</b> on <b>April 29, 2004, 11:34:07 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I wouldn&#039;t say we had most people leaving FoT for other servers etc... Certainly some have left, and it did have an effect. I&#039;d be a liar if I said otherwise. <br /><br />We had a stumble with a few deciding to seek greener pastures, and that&#039;s thier decision. I&#039;ve always been of the mind that just because the paint is chipped, a cracked window or two and the gutters broken on a house, you don&#039;t go buy a new one, you just fix up the one ya have.<br /><br />Others live in a disposable world, and would rather make a fast easy change. <br /><br />Just a different point of view between those people, and the rest who remain in FoT now. <br /><br />I would say the same thing is occuring in Forsaken, just at different levels. Does it mean they are done as a guild? That I can&#039;t say, it really depends on who remains to determine thier path now, and if they want to make it work.<br /><br />The Leaders and officers of guild do certainly set the course, and direction of a guild, but it takes the members to get the job done. </div>
