					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Ahnnisa Celeborne</b> on <b>May 01, 2004, 10:21:51 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">At risk of jumping into the middle of a flame war (not really cuz I really don&#039;t think I&#039;ll repsond regardless of who replies to this post)....<br /><br />I&#039;ve hated Forsaken since early 2003, firstly for training over my Kael arena raid to get to Vindi and laughing about it in guild speak, and with every instance where they ran over whatever guild or group I was with in whatever zone I was in many times later. As a guild they had few ethics. <br /><br />Unfortunately I had good friends in Forsaken. And finally, after arguing with one of  my closest friends forever about it, he convinced me to join Forsaken and see how they had &quot;changed&quot;. About 6 weeks later I left EQ and put my account up for sale, I was so disgusted with the game and with myself for being apart of them. Fortunately I calmed down 5 months later and returned to EQ, now happy with my current guild.<br /><br />All this said... I still respect Forsaken, if for nothing else, then for the these <b>facts</b>:<br /><br /><b>A)</b> Rogosh, &quot;Mr No Personality a**hole&quot; that he was, knew how to lead a raid.  There is no other person I have seen that could accomplish the things he could get accomplished.<br /><br /><b>B)</b> On all of your top ten lists, no other guild cracks the top 5 that can claim pure recruitment as the sole means of growth. Every other top 5 guild has swallowed other guilds or merged. That in itself is a sign of people acknowledging that Forsaken has/had the skill and the ability necessary to draw in quality recruits (it was after all most every other guild above Forsaken that were hitting Rogosh with requests to merge, not the other way around).<br /><br /><b>C)</b> No other guild in the top 5 was able to reach PoTime in the short period of game time it took Forsaken. No other guild in the top 5 has been able to sustain the consistent drive that Forsaken did in getting to Time. Forsaken never went on holiday or experienced temporary mass drops in membership or raid capability. They always moved forward.<br /><br /><b>D)</b> No other top 5 guild can truthfully claim to have done more events with fewer numbers and more ORIGINAL strategy than Forsaken, with the exception of perhaps Ascent. And I would temper that by saying that had Forsaken been where Ascent was at the time of PoP release, it would have been a very different world. But Ascent had the luxury of being born long before Forsaken.<br /><br />Hate Forsaken for whatever reason you wish, it&#039;s your right as a human. But by the very same means in which you measure greatness in EQ, by the loot you hoarde and the flags you acquire, by the childish way that many of you cherish in game accomplishments over real-life accomplishments.... you <b>OWE</b> Forsaken the credit they deserve. The things Forsaken has done to get to the 4th spot on your list, they did far more efficiently, far quicker, than those 3 above them.<br /><br />If I had to rate the top 5 guilds based on ability, on over all accomplishment, Forsaken would have to rank 1st.<br /><br />As I dance on Forsakens grave, I also raise a toast to them, and actually am secretly kinda rooting for them to bounce back now that a majority of the people I so despised are gone from their ranks. <br /><br />/salute Forsaken peeps</div>
					<br />
