					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Ahnnisa,<br /><br />      While I can appreciate your fervor, I can&#039;t help but wonder how much crack you smoked before making that post. <br /><br /><br />A. Just because you haven&#039;t seen it doesn&#039;t mean it doesn&#039;t exsist. Hell I&#039;ve never seen anyone get struck by lightning, but I&#039;m sure it happens. <br /><br />B. No other Top Guild on Rodcet has been the resting place of the rejects from every other guild. When people are refused or kicked out of Ascent, DA/EiE, FoT they end up with Forsaken......That&#039;s not really recruitment....that&#039;s taking the scraps from the table, and being thankful for it.<br /><br />C. Forsaken took the longest to get to Time. PoP was released at the same time for everyone.....It seems to me that Ascent got there first.....So Ascent did it in the shortest amount of time.   How you can consider being the last of the top 4 to get there the &quot;fastest&quot; I don&#039;t know....Probably an effect of the time distortion the crack gives you. <br /><br />D. Show me some hard numbers and evidence.....That&#039;s all speculation without it. Lets not forget Forsaken&#039;s method of getting &quot;Original strategies&quot;.....Lets have a Rogue or druid follow another guild on a raid, and watch how they kill a mob....Emulate it, and kill the mob for themselves.<br /><br />Oh, by the way.....Forsaken was formed a few months after Ascent was....so Ascent isn&#039;t all that much older. Lets also not forget that within weeks of forming Ascent was competing with AoD for top mobs. The first 6 months or so Forsaken had an Alliance with Warlords of Wrath, or Habingers of Storms (I forget)<br /><br /><br />How you can rate Forsaken as #1 for ability and accomplishment I have no idea. They have been, are, and always will be third rate.  When Forsaken starts getting some server firsts then perhaps they can start ranking at the top.<br /><br />Forsaken has never done anything quicker or more efficently than other guilds. Hell Forsaken is YEARS older than Fires of Time, and still is left sucking tit while others move forward. <br /><br />I like Forsaken....I was one of the forces that created it. I like many of the people in it. I&#039;ve remained friends with Rogosh through the years.....<br /><br />However, you are way off base, and your facts are pure speculation where they aren&#039;t 100% fucking idiocy.<br /><br /><br />Cloudskipper 65 Cleric<br />Cloudsmasher 65 Berserker</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Delheru</b> on <b>May 01, 2004, 11:15:11 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">What&#039;s this Ahnnisa person smoking? I mean really.<br /><br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">All this said... I still respect Forsaken, if for nothing else, then for the these <b>facts</b>:<br /><br /><b>A)</b> Rogosh, &quot;Mr No Personality a**hole&quot; that he was, knew how to lead a raid.  There is no other person I have seen that could accomplish the things he could get accomplished..</div><br /><br />Amazing. You&#039;ve attended a lot of raids run by, say, Jeet or myself or Fignutn? Because the logic of saying that &quot;I only attended #4 guilds raids, and they were the best I&#039;ev been on, so they must really be #1&quot; is some pretty trippy logic.<br /><br /><br /><br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote"> On all of your top ten lists, no other guild cracks the top 5 that can claim pure recruitment as the sole means of growth. Every other top 5 guild has swallowed other guilds or merged. That in itself is a sign of people acknowledging that Forsaken has/had the skill and the ability necessary to draw in quality recruits (it was after all most every other guild above Forsaken that were hitting Rogosh with requests to merge, not the other way around).</div><br /><br />Guilds broke down trying to compete with us, and then their officers gathered their wits and apped to us. Many of these recruits had lead guilds that ate Forsaken for breakfast (AD, AoD to name a few). Only thing missing was the lamentation of their women, and that might have been because I don&#039;t have sounds on in EQ.<br /><br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote"><b>C)</b> No other guild in the top 5 was able to reach PoTime in the short period of game time it took Forsaken.</div><br /><br />What? Starting from when? From when Avatar of Earth was at 15% health?<br /><br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">No other guild in the top 5 has been able to sustain the consistent drive that Forsaken did in getting to Time.</div><br /><br />I must have missed something. FoT stopped for a second, but only time we ever slowed down was because Rathe was UNBEATABLE. DA/EiE never even slowed down since Rathe was killable when they reached it. Sure their progress was bit sluggish, but I do believe it was still faster than Forsaken.<br /><br /><br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">Forsaken never went on holiday or experienced temporary mass drops in membership or raid capability. They always moved forward.</div><br /><br />Never noticed this happening to us, DA/EiE or FoT either. I mean what makes this so special?<br /><br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">No other top 5 guild can truthfully claim to have done more events with fewer numbers and more ORIGINAL strategy than Forsaken, with the exception of perhaps Ascent.</div><br /><br />We have done more events with fewer numbers and more original strategy than Forsaken. Last Quarm kill was with 42. Come on guys, go for it!<br /><br /><br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">And I would temper that by saying that had Forsaken been where Ascent was at the time of PoP release, it would have been a very different world.</div><br /><br />Yeah and if all their members had been created with 100% shielding, things would have gone better too. Or if they had killed Quarm first, then they would have beat PoTime before anyone else! Gosh. <br /><br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote"> But Ascent had the luxury of being born long before Forsaken.</div><br /><br />No we had the luxury of having way better leadership and core members.<br /><br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">Hate Forsaken for whatever reason you wish, it&#039;s your right as a human.</div><br /><br />I don&#039;t hate them by any means. I just find the pedestal you put them on really funny, since you obviously have absolutely no clue about the high end game in EQ. Forsaken was not downtrodden except when their ass got whooped back in line by a stronger guild. They were #4 because their dedication, skill of memberbase, skill of leadership, playtime etc came out on average as... wow... #4! Not #1, #4. Judge people by their deeds, not by your own mental images of what must be true.<br /><br /><br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">you <b>OWE</b> Forsaken the credit they deserve. The things Forsaken has done to get to the 4th spot on your list, they did far more efficiently, far quicker, than those 3 above them.</div><br /><br />If they did them any better, they wouldn&#039;t have been stuck at #4. FoT went through so mayn ups and downs that the miracle of sticking around was theirs. How Forsaken failed to pass them was quite amazing, but fail they did.<br /><br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">If I had to rate the top 5 guilds based on ability, on over all accomplishment, Forsaken would have to rank 1st.</div><br /><br />Based on what? You&#039;ve never been closer to an Ascent raid then being in PoTranq when we&#039;ve beein an elemental plane I bet. I would be surprised if that wasn&#039;t the case of your insider knowledge of DA/EiE or FoT for that matter.<br /><br /><br />I mean no hate on Forsaken, but what on earth did you conjure this up from?</div>
					<br />
