					Post by: <b>Grem</b> on <b>May 01, 2004, 11:33:37 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">HAHA WHOA hold on there!<br /><br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">All this said... I still respect Forsaken, if for nothing else, then for the these <b>facts</b>:<br /><br /><b>A)</b> Rogosh, &quot;Mr No Personality a**hole&quot; that he was, knew how to lead a raid.  There is no other person I have seen that could accomplish the things he could get accomplished.<br /></div><br /><br />Mr. &quot;I&#039;ll disband this fucking guild if we don&#039;t have Coirnav or Rathe killed by xxx!&quot;  That&#039;s personality.  I mean, it&#039;s stupid, but it&#039;s a personality.  Mostly I quoted this part, cause almost nothing you put on this list is facts.  And you must of seen very few leaders in your day, if Rogosh is your grand standard of accomplishment.<br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote"><b>B)</b> On all of your top ten lists, no other guild cracks the top 5 that can claim pure recruitment as the sole means of growth. Every other top 5 guild has swallowed other guilds or merged. That in itself is a sign of people acknowledging that Forsaken has/had the skill and the ability necessary to draw in quality recruits (it was after all most every other guild above Forsaken that were hitting Rogosh with requests to merge, not the other way around).<br /></div><br /><br />Yes, it&#039;s well known that Honch has had an offer on the table for well over a year now, that any time Forsaken wants to merge, just send him a tell!  Are you fucking kidding me?  DA/EiE requesting a merge?  They need more people sitting outside Time?  FoT I can sort of see, Eelyen was a tool.  Forsaken&#039;s advanced recruitment policy...uh, I&#039;ll take your word on that...I can&#039;t remember last time I said &quot;wow, so and so app&#039;ed to Forsaken&quot;.<br /><br /><br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote"><b>C)</b> No other guild in the top 5 was able to reach PoTime in the short period of game time it took Forsaken. No other guild in the top 5 has been able to sustain the consistent drive that Forsaken did in getting to Time. Forsaken never went on holiday or experienced temporary mass drops in membership or raid capability. They always moved forward.<br /></div><br /><br />That&#039;s because they always had somewhere to move.  If you&#039;re using PoTime as a measuring stick.  I guess Ascent took 3 years to get there? DA took almost 5?  That&#039;s laughable.  Forsaken accomplished probably the least.  They found one spot on the top ten list, and stuck there.  They didn&#039;t move up or down much.  They never killed something before the people ahead of them.  Unimpressive.  Interesting facts though, considering they&#039;re 100% based on opinions<br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote"><b>D)</b> No other top 5 guild can truthfully claim to have done more events with fewer numbers and more ORIGINAL strategy than Forsaken, with the exception of perhaps Ascent. And I would temper that by saying that had Forsaken been where Ascent was at the time of PoP release, it would have been a very different world. But Ascent had the luxury of being born long before Forsaken.<br /></div><br /><br />One has nothing to do with the other.  On top of that, it&#039;s more opinions.  On top of THAT, there are members in Forsaken that have played as long, or longer, than people in Ascent.  What took them so fucking long, eh?<br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote"> you <b>OWE</b> Forsaken the credit they deserve. The things Forsaken has done to get to the 4th spot on your list, they did far more efficiently, far quicker, than those 3 above them.<br /><br />If I had to rate the top 5 guilds based on ability, on over all accomplishment, Forsaken would have to rank 1st.<br /><br /></div><br /><br />You must be on some drugs.  Stupid drugs.  Guess what 4th place gets in the Olympics?  Not a damn thing.  How can you say Forsaken has done the things the 3 guilds above them have done, only better, when they haven&#039;t even engaged some of them?  And when they did reach those mobs, they had spoilers, strats, people on the raid that have already done the encounters.  <br /><br />On over all accomplishment, Forsaken skipped doing Fear at level 50, doing Trak and NToV at 60.  Doing VT at 60.  Let me break it down to you Barney style.  Guild A(A as in Ascent, but let&#039;s not be bias, could very well be DA), has 100 cookies.  Guild B(Bitch stfu you&#039;re stupid) has 4 cookies.<br /><br />It take the same amount of time for Guild A and Guild B to eat 1 cookie.  Guild B has eaten 75% of it&#039;s cookies!  Guild A only ate 1% :(  Guild B must be a better cookie eater than Guild A, right?  No, so shut up.<br /><br />Now to make it clear, I think Forsaken has done a fine job, and I never believed the bad rap they were given.  Them harassing our apps is kind of lame, but, meh, I can understand.  But to say they&#039;re number one over all?  You&#039;re one of those people that saw the first Matrix and said it was the greatest trilogy ever, huh?</div>
