					Post by: <b>Kinladar</b> on <b>May 02, 2004, 11:01:10 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I wouldn&#039;t lump us into the same situation as Forsaken.<br /><br />We had some peeps want to server transfer, a total of 5 people. Thier choice.<br /><br />Had 2 leave over reportedly not able to work with a potential app that was accepted, a case of bad communications that could have been resolved, but such is life.<br /><br />One left who has returned as well.<br /><br />I don&#039;t see any parallels when Forsaken lost most of thier top leadership, and has lost many members. I have had some people be honest with me and tell me they did at first put in apps with other guild when this all broke, but are retracting them now. Willing to go the distance and see it through.<br /><br />I can&#039;t say I would blame them for doing the inquiry into other guilds, when the stuff went down last week, some things were badly handled in those events. On my part as well as anyone&#039;s.<br /><br />But in the end, the core remains, we&#039;re still finishing up things that were on the table prior, and still getting more people flagged for Kod Taz, and soon to beyond. There are some people who have worked thier asses off to help keep that going as well, people like Thebobo, Valcare, Arweyn, Cuthul, Suntuz, Reyem, Hamek, Shylai, and so many others who already had the stuff, yet volunteer to get others through it all. These people are the reason FoT is not going anywhere. The dedication they have to helping others, and helping will be what sees us through.<br /><br />I can&#039;t thank them enough for what they have done in the past, and what they continue to do now.</div>
