					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Zerxes</b> on <b>July 08, 2004, 11:53:27 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Callon $txt[176] July 07, 2004, 06:17:54 pm</div><div class="quote">I&#039;d love to see a 2nd viable alternative to advancement besides elementals, but it doesn&#039;t exist right now.  You need at least elemental geared tanks to do much of anything in GoD.  Maybe OoW will offer another path.  Nah, I doubt it.  :badhairday:<br /></div><br /><br />OoW will raise the level cap to 70 which will likely help you guys over the hump in getting into the EP&#039;s.&nbsp; Raising the level cap always trivializes content to a certain extent - what used to take a full raid of 72 will likely only take 50 level 70 people.&nbsp; This is assuming of course that spells are readily available to casters, which is a HUGE &quot;IF.&quot;<br /><br />Also, while this may or may not help TA, I read a report from the Guild Summit that said that Time-quality gear is coming to a LDoN merchant near you!&nbsp; :banghead2:</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Callon</b> on <b>July 08, 2004, 12:59:22 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">OoW will raise the level cap to 70 which will likely help you guys over the hump in getting into the EP&#039;s.&nbsp; Raising the level cap always trivializes content to a certain extent - what used to take a full raid of 72 will likely only take 50 level 70 people.&nbsp; This is assuming of course that spells are readily available to casters, which is a HUGE &quot;IF.&quot;</div><br /><br />I don&#039;t want it to be trivialized at all.&nbsp; I&#039;m concerned about the L70 cap doing just that.&nbsp; The big problem for us with progression right now is not the difficulty of the mobs.&nbsp; It&#039;s the difficulty of finding the damn mobs UP!&nbsp; This week we&#039;ve searched in vain for flag mobs.&nbsp; Last night they were all dead or about to be killed by other guilds except Agnarr.&nbsp; We didn&#039;t have the wizards on at our usual start time of 8:30 est, which is already too late for many mobs anyway because so many guilds are raiding by 5-7 pm.&nbsp; We&#039;re more casual, have busy jobs and family and whatnot, and we start when the core of our raid team gets on.&nbsp; In effect our time zone starts later than some guilds.&nbsp; So stuff isn&#039;t up.&nbsp; <br /><br />Anyway, finally closer to 9 we&#039;ve gotten a couple more wizards and we&#039;re up to 3 of them, so we decide to try it.&nbsp; Oops, too late.&nbsp; RoS is in BoT now and killing Agnarr.&nbsp; They&#039;ve been in elems for months, but apparently it&#039;s still worth it to go back and kill flag mobs for loot and twink flags.&nbsp; That&#039;s one of the biggest problems right now with progression.&nbsp; The constant backflagging is bad enough.&nbsp; Then many mobs die even if they&#039;re not really needed for backflagging so people can flag their twinks, get the loot, etc.&nbsp; I don&#039;t mean to pick on RoS.&nbsp; It&#039;s a game problem.&nbsp; Progression for guilds like ours is blocked by guilds for whom the content is trivial. <br /><br />Flag mobs aren&#039;t up nearly often enough, drop loot that people would want to farm, and progression in EQ is often determined by how early in the evening you can log on, not by whether your guild has the skill and power to take down the mobs.&nbsp; Not that that&#039;s anything new in EQ, but it&#039;s stupid as hell and needs to change.<br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">Also, while this may or may not help TA, I read a report from the Guild Summit that said that Time-quality gear is coming to a LDoN merchant near you!</div><br /><br />This would be a huge mistake.&nbsp; I don&#039;t care how long you sit there and grind normal ldons in your L65 groups.&nbsp; You should NEVER be able to buy time quality gear for so little risk.&nbsp; The 1492 pt armor there is plenty good enough for something you can get just by doing ldon normals over and over.&nbsp; Putting in better stuff would hose risk versus reward.&nbsp; If they want to improve the gear available with adventure points, that&#039;s fine, but it should be a separate set of points earned from harder adventures.&nbsp; Expedition style zones put in GoD could have supported it.&nbsp; If they added new instanced zones in OoW where you could earn points for better loot, fine.&nbsp; As long as the risk vs. reward makes sense, they could perhaps make it so good gear doesn&#039;t take quite so damn many adventures to get, too.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Grem</b> on <b>July 08, 2004, 01:13:41 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Callon $txt[176] July 08, 2004, 12:59:22 pm</div><div class="quote"><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote"> We&#039;re more casual, have busy jobs and family and whatnot, and we start when the core of our raid team gets on.  In effect our time zone starts later than some guilds.  So stuff isn&#039;t up.  <br /></div><br /><br />I have a busier job and a family, beat that! But still I&#039;m considered a hardcore player..=p</div></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Callon</b> on <b>July 08, 2004, 03:04:24 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">I have a busier job and a family, beat that! But still I&#039;m considered a hardcore player..=p</div><br /><br />I knew someone would take issue with the job/family comment, hence my remark about just playing on a different timetable than some guilds.&nbsp; Think of it that way.&nbsp; If your guild starts raiding at 6pm est, you will generally find more targets up than if your guild can&#039;t start until 9.<br /><br />So...&nbsp; :bitch:</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
