					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Domaris</b> on <b>July 21, 2004, 01:24:17 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I actually have nothing against people beating us to targets, that is the way it has always been and we eventually find mobs we need up. My point was just the fact that a guild used others to backflag their apps then basically did not return the favor. <br /><br />However we are at the same point now where we have so many apps and regular members at raids having anyone tag along for a flag, unless we have done the mob before and most of our members have it already, is a pretty big hindrance. I see that point and agree totally, your guild members should always come before tag alongs. But when its a flag for *one* guild member, and you blow off other people and guilds who helped you get where you are - that is the part that bothered me. I see some of the reasoning behind it and I am not an officer so don&#039;t get the tells asking for tag along flags, we have never had more then maybe 1 group at a time of non guildies or apps I think on raids, but I also don&#039;t agree with the *Hey you let me tag along before can I bring 20 of my closest friends?* approach either. That is taking advantage, and I would tell em to take a hike in that instance as well. </div>
					<br />
