					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Still trying to figger out how any one guild can accuse any other guild(s) of wrong doing when it comes to &quot;cock blocking&quot; zones/mobs/events, removing mobs &quot;for fun&quot; that others &quot;need&quot;, etc.. All of ya&#039;s have done it. &#039;Fess up to it and move on, stop pointing all these fingers, geez.<br /><br />Go back to Nov 1999 - Mar 2000. How many people in the top 5 guilds today took part in the Nagafen/Lady Vox wars, running right over others, and then keeping them down once the science of the raid became established? And later in Kael Drakkel? It&#039;s been a part of the game since the beginning and is certainly present today. You as an individual may not have knowlingly or willingly taken part in blocking others, but as a whole few guilds in or attempting to break the top 10 are innocent of it. As a few have already said, part of the problem is game mechanics.<br /><br />Another part is that yer dealing with humans (tho this could be debated with some). And decisions to take down mobs, whether to block another guild and disguise it as a backflagging attempt or a sincere effort to flag people, falls to individual humans. There will be a million reasons/excuses for every decision. <br /><br />I remember turning my guild chat off one day while in Forsaken because I didn&#039;t want to see the couple of idiots out of the bunch bragging and laughing about how they wiped someone elses Kael arena Right raid to get AoW. Two of those particular members is in Ascent, one in FoT, and another in DA today. I also recall being blocked out of Ssra by whatever the hell FoT was before they absorbed everyone and became FoT. So to simply point out one guild or two amongst the 5+ that do it is just wrong. It&#039;s not like any guild is completely innocent of any of it. <br /><br />In Conviction I recall vividly being over run by RoS in PoAir and somehow, even tho we were CLEARLY in the zone, set up, and engaging mobs... RoS was able to pull a GM into the zone and order all Conviction to leave the zone or face GM punishment?!?!?!?! RoS wasn&#039;t even IN the zone when we began to engage the trash mobs.<br /><br />/shrug<br /><br />I think it was best stated in this thread by the person who simply replied:<br /><br />&quot;Welcome to life...&quot;<br /><br />Now get over it. <br /><br /></div>
