					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">i&#039;ve been hearing alot about DA/EiE passing Ascent as of late, and while possible, there&#039;s one thing i want to coment on... it seems to me (not being on the server anymore, with only second hand information) that Ascent is having similar, though maybe a more severe version of the problems my own guild is having atm... <br /><br />while trying to complete Txevu with around 54-ish people, so they dont have people sitting out / too many people in Tacvi,&nbsp; they&#039;re maybe finding it difficult to complete the events in the zone with this number of people. (pure speculation, based on what my own guild is going through atm)&nbsp; while DA/EiE have ample numbers of people, and they will have a much easier time with some events, being that they have more numbers and higher dps, if nothing more. <br /><br /> i dont believe the rumors i&#039;ve heard about Ascent dieing, or being dead.&nbsp; but it&#039;s alot harder to complete an event with 40 people, that another guild can do with 60-70 (not saying thats how much DA/EiE raid with, because i dont know... just saying~)&nbsp; and i honestly think the events in Txevu might be scaled more twards the higher number raids, as opposed to the 54 man instanced raids that Ascent is trying to keep their number&#039;s around..... just something to consider when evaluating weather or not a guild is &#039;dieing&#039; </div>
