					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Ascent just changed a bit in composition after we got our guildinvite to WoW beta.<br /><br />Most of the old players had just had enough of EQ, and moved on. The numbers lost weren&#039;t really huge, but did include a major portion of the older players.<br />Old EQ players will probably recognize a lot more players from the WoW guild roster than from the current Ascent roster. However most of the WoW players<br />weren&#039;t very active in EQ for a long time, so as such the hit Ascent took shouldn&#039;t have been too huge.<br /><br />People with high level characters in WoW &lt;Ascent&gt;:<br />Delheru, Vesi, Lumilla, Reia, Baelt, Kariena, Bippon, Dyvim, Braelyia, Sethric, Bagbokk, Celerity, Basar, Tyal, Xanthorian, Chauey, Thun, Lighting, Mcbashin etc etc<br /><br />Others with chars in the WoW guild include people like Mallagin who don&#039;t really have much time to play WoW either.<br /><br />Many of those people haven&#039;t played EQ in significant amounts for quite a while (Reia, Bippon, Sethric, Brae, Basar, Tyal, Thun, Lighting) and others weren&#039;t<br />even in EQ Ascent (Dyvim, Bagbokk, Celerity). In that sense the number of people lost wasn&#039;t big. The guild just has to rearrange itself a bit due to the<br />officer inbalance with Me/Vesi/Reia/Brae/Sethric/Tyal in WoW  (though at least Vesi hasn&#039;t technically retired from EQ). </div>
