					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Big time derailer incoming . . . <br /><br />We need information . . . information . . . information<br /><br />So Del, give us the scoop thus far on WoW - if you want to be polite and maintain the integrity of this thread by starting another, by all means do it hehe (probably best if you did).&nbsp; I know that the &quot;endgame&quot; isn&#039;t in the beta yet (at least not all of it).&nbsp; But what are your impressions thus far?&nbsp; Is this a game EQers (especially those who thrive on the raiding aspect of EQ) are going to like?&nbsp; Is it going to have &quot;staying power&quot;?&nbsp; I know people complain its too easy to level, but it seems Blizzard is relying on the fact that getting to the max level will be so much fun, people will enjoy starting new characters and doing it again . . . <br /><br />Anyone else who is IN the Beta (please, I don&#039;t want second hand information from what somebody has read on some board, I&#039;ve read plenty of that), and has a background of raiding in EQ (I&#039;m not interested in the trade-skiller&#039;s perspective or in the perspective of the little casual guy who likes to group with 3-4 of his friends a couple of times a week), feel free to respond as well (probably best in a new thread).&nbsp; I&#039;m just hoping to get the perspective from the high-end raider, because quite frankly, Afterlife, Fires of Heaven, etc. have all been pretty damm silent thus far.<br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Callon</b> on <b>August 10, 2004, 12:30:02 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">Keep in mind the Brewmasters got all their flag kills solo no help, they may<br />be slower in advancing but they do stuff on their own.</div><br /><br />I think that&#039;s how the majority of guilds are advancing.&nbsp; I know almost all of TA/JH&#039;s kills have been on our own.&nbsp; Ok, ok, that&#039;s already 2 guilds.&nbsp;  :)&nbsp; But we always raid together and we&#039;ve left it that way rather than keeping recruitment open to bring more into TA.&nbsp; I don&#039;t feel like our advancement is discredited by sometimes letting some people from other guilds tag with us.&nbsp; That&#039;s just good business.&nbsp; We&#039;re trying to save each other some backflagging pains and in guilds with more casual players like ours, backflagging can really be ugly.&nbsp; You kill a flag mob several times and you&#039;ve still got a significant number of raiders who don&#039;t have the flag yet.&nbsp; <br /><br />Not that we&#039;re top 10 anyway...&nbsp; 8)&nbsp; <br /><br />btw, I think Brews seem to advance slowly mainly because they did the VT thing, which is cool.&nbsp; They&#039;ve explained more than once that that&#039;s just what they wanted to do as a guild, regardless of how others measure progression.&nbsp; So good for them.&nbsp;  :cwm20:</div>
					<br />
