					Post by: <b>Delheru</b> on <b>November 09, 2004, 01:15:06 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Jeet $txt[176] November 09, 2004, 12:39:29 pm</div><div class="quote"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Leeandra Sheerslayer $txt[176] November 09, 2004, 03:25:52 am</div><div class="quote">and there is no limit on how low they will go to do it.</div><br />If you think your guild now has a shining history of morality, you are pretty naive.</div><br />We actually never did anything that bad.<br /><br />Hell I don&#039;t recall a single incident of training against AoD/AL either way around. Nor against DA/EiE, Arirang or FoT for that matter. Certainly not something done on purpose and condoned (or actually executed) by the leadership of the guild. I don&#039;t recall any guild ever intentionally training us, and I have always been extremely strict on someone training. To me it always gave the feel of someone scoring 1595 in SAT looking at their neighbors just in case someone might get the last one right. It&#039;s unnecessary, demeaning and you frankly are more likely to lower your score than to improve it.</div>
