					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Jeet $txt[176] November 09, 2004, 04:26:18 pm</div><div class="quote">I guess we&#039;re going to have to agree to disagree then Del.<br />The bottom line for me - which I have always tried to influence on my guild and the alliance in general - is treat people how you want to be treated.</div><br />Well we never did anything cheesy or downright forbidden. We had our set of rules, always abided by them and made them pretty damn clear to anyone that wanted to compete with us. I never thought the rules had any sort of real bias toward us either, but were rather quite neutral.<br /><br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">I can respect the fact that you did much of what you did out of competition.  That doesnt mean I think it was all kocher or on that moral highpath.  Wasnt all that long ago we reciprocated this treatment to your remaining guildmembers (pressured and rushed them), and they obviously didn&#039;t find it very kocher either (even tried to strike a deal with us).</div><br />You know the guild would not have complained in the old days, even if you were winning. We might have considered dealing with you, but mostly we&#039;d have just focused on getting past you. I don&#039;t think most would have minded it really.<br /><br />Anyway when the hell did we do a lot of pressuring or rushing against you? We never ran past your full force, and SCd past you once.</div>
