					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Garadan</b> on <b>November 11, 2004, 11:24:36 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Most of the people you see posting their good bye posts on our boards are people who havent been playing actively for awhile. And now that the new games have dropped they are just making it official by offering their accounts for sale to guild members first before they go to PA. <br /><br />We are or have been in a rebuilding stage, although I wouldnt so much say we are now. We arent of course the super power that we once were. However I doubt it will ever come to that again considering losing so many top end players and due to changes in the game ie instancing, brings on a whole new aspect. <br /><br />I will boldly say though that even with the group of members we have now we still have accomplished more then FoT. We are 1 kill away from beating Inku&#039;ta. And while thats 1 expansion old, its still no joke. In regards to OoW we have been learning raid trials, although its a bit hard to do those with sub par numbers and gear. So a lot of re-equiping raids are usually done, M&#039;shas, Ink, Ikinniz etc..<br /><br />As far as the train frenzy thats going on lately, we as officers in Ascent do not support that or allow that from our members. I can safely say that any raid that I have lead it has never happened. The accusation about Draybard was a bit wrong, considering he argo&#039;d the mob first and was pulling it back to our camp when several members of the FoT raid tried to intercept... turned out to be death move for them /shrug. I wouldnt say thats us training.... however when someone grabs a handful of mobs and runs into the main body of a raid... ya thats a train...ie the SS&#039;s. Sometimes its hard to swallow the pill knowing you have been out pulled, out maneuvered.</div>
					<br />
