					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Slayyerr</b> on <b>November 24, 2004, 12:14:24 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I don&#039;t say much here. But I would not rank UoP 10 just because of lack of activity. Everyone is lacking participation atm due to EQ / WoW. I used to be in UoP and do not have the best of terms with them but as far as rankings go, until you surpass or equal what a guild accomplishes you cannot be ahead of them. UoP has a FR kill and has EP on farm status. The top 3 remain the same as it will for the next few weeks until we see how things play out with the new games. Conviction and RoS still behind DA/EiE, AScent, FoT and no one I see behind atm seem to making any progress to show a surge past the top 5. Once you get past the top&nbsp; there isn&#039;t much happening as I see it. The top 5 are all farming what they can and gearing up re-building (as is everyone) and seeing what happens. UoP remains 7 below Ruination/whoever else they raid with until you get a GoD kill. The next month will tell the story of EQ. I forsee server mergers coming to reduce the server numbers and populate what remains. The EQ will survive on those numbers. Rankings is all moot realy unless you are 1 or 2 IMO. They lead the way and show everyone else what it is and sometimes how it is done. </div>
					<br />
