					Post by: <b>Slayyerr</b> on <b>November 25, 2004, 05:48:07 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I said you base it on what they have accomplished. DA/EiE has surpassed Ascent in GoD, thus they are at the top (for the moment). You cannot put Hegemony,Forsaken, or the others because they no longer exist as a guild. There may people that still hold the tag, but that does not mean the guild as a whole exists. Like I said the battle is really among the top 3 for the moment, because they are the hard core raiders and can accomplish more things in a shorter amount of time. But I would not rate a guild that has just entered EP&#039;s above a guild that is still active (alothough not very) and has a FR kill. Until Brew, OA, or the others do that then I would assume they could make an argument for surpassing them. The next few weeks will tell the tell for most of the top 10. Some WILL fold and some will carry on. It is just EQ&#039;s nature. But history has shown that the Top 5 and I would include UoP as a guild that has been on the server for quite sometime and still survive. I do agree thou it has been long overdue for a change of Leadership there, which had been ask for by some  :cwm34: more than 6-8 months ago. Guilds must have active leadership to survive, along with the core to help carry them.</div>
