					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Zorlo</b> on <b>November 26, 2004, 04:58:52 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">FoT is nowhere near Ascent atm, so there is no real &quot;fight&quot; for 2nd.&nbsp; </div><br /><br />Ok, i come from absolutley 0 knowledge of the two guilds other then what i pick up on here, and from friends i know. However, every single thread i read, one person will say something along the lines of &quot;EiE/DA is the best by far, and FoT and Ascent are fighting for 2nd&quot;. Then, maybe one FoT person will post something about how they agree or whatever. And 500 Ascent people post declaring that ascent is #2, and FoT isnt anywhere near. Listen, i respect Ascent as much as anyone, but my question is: Has &quot;new&quot; Ascent caught &quot;old&quot; Ascent? I saw a post a while ago from Snake, about how &quot;as soon as they get together the people, they will do Inktu&#039;ta&quot; or something, well i mean, as soon as i get together the people i plan to Time flag myself... The facts that are obvious to me are: Neither Ascent nor FoT raids Txevu, regardless of whether or not some are flagged. They both raid Qvic on a regular basis. PG trials are a mystery to me, and whether or not Ascent has more then FoT or whatever, i dont know, but neither are Anguish flagged, and neither are close. About a month ago, i heard that Ascent can not clear Time as fast as FoT, i dont know if that is still true. However, i wont be surprised if an ascent person posts something about how they cleared Time in 3 hours a year ago. Additionally, Ascent is clearly taking more apps then FoT, typically at a lower or equal standard. <br /><br />My point is this: Fires of Time and Ascent are both great guilds, experiencing new content, and raiding on a higher level then 95 percent of the game. However, the constant bickering about who is 2nd and who is 3rd is pointless, untill a more concrete distinction arises, not like &quot;Ascent will beat Ink next week if we have numbers&quot;. You cannot compare Old Ascent to Present Fot. Past Ascent accomplishments might as well be forgotten, untill they are caught and passed. <br /><br />Please though, like i said, i&#039;m not in either guild, so if Ascent has apparently beaten a bunch of trials and soon going to kill everything in tacvi, or whatever, let me know. </div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Ssnakess</b> on <b>November 26, 2004, 06:51:04 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">&quot;New&quot; Ascent has killed a PG raid, which FoT has not. &quot;New&quot; Ascent has nearly beaten Inktu&#039;ta (final named 29%), when FoT has not even killed the first named of the zone.<br /><br />Once we beat Inktu&#039;ta, we simply need 1 real named, and 4 pushover named kills in Txevu, and we have caught &quot;Old&quot; Ascent.<br /><br />Why everyone insists on calling Ascent new and old is beyond me, we didn&#039;t reform, we lost as many people as FoT has lost recently. Why not divide FoT into two timeframes? I realize that someone will insist its because Ascent changed leadership,&nbsp; but in that case, then the current EiE is the &quot;new&quot; EiE too?<br /><br />The only similarity between FoT and Ascent atm, is we both farm sha&#039;s. After that, the comparison ends.<br /><br />And yes, you cannot compare Ascent prior to OoW with FoT now. But you can compare current guilds, and we are still well ahead of them.</div>
