					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Dwalion SoulVoid $txt[176] November 27, 2004, 10:09:17 pm</div><div class="quote">RN Top of all time.<br />1.  Avatars of Discord<br />2.  Ascent<br />3.  Altered Destiny<br />4.  EiE<br />5.  Eastern Keep<br />6.  DA<br />7.  FoT<br />8.  Harbingers of Storms<br />9.  Arcane Legacy<br />10.  Dragon Knight<br />11.  Mythmakers<br />12.  Dragon Force<br />13.  Conviction<br />14.  Reign of Swords<br />15.  Exiled Legion<br />16.  Ancient Souls<br />17.  Axiom Shift<br />18.  Forsaken  <br />19.  Union of Power<br />20.  Circle of Sol</div><br />lmao<br /><br />AoD as #1?<br />For what? Reigning the server for the original game (with a non too insignificant ally I might add). Then struggling for top dog position<br />with an even bigger alliance for one expansion, and then being #2 to Ascent in two more. <br /><br />Ascent reigned the server longer and did very well serverwide. I definitely wouldn&#039;t even consider that a competition. Had AoD totally<br />dominated Kunark, we might have something to talk about, but that was hardly the case after all.<br /><br />Putting AD in front of DA/EiE seems strange to me as well. What exactly have they done besides an allied Trakanon? One hit wonder at<br />its best... I&#039;d say:<br /><br />1. Ascent<br />2. AoD/AL<br />3. DA/EiE<br />4. Arirang<br />5. EK<br />6. FoT<br />7. HoS<br />8. Conviction<br />9. AD<br />10. Axiom and its predecessors<br /><br />Obviously Conviction and FoT can only move up, while most around them are immobile.</div>
