					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">most of these people, are prolly juts bullshiting so they can think they aqre &quot;uber&quot;. lets say you have 4 clerics which u need. 1 tank for FR 2 slowers assuming it will nto stick on first try that gives you 7 people assusiming thats all u use for those classes. that leaves 5 DPS. very doubtful you will drop him with 2 groups... i saw DA/EiE drop fire nameds with 10 they did it eas y but very very long fights and FR is signifigantly harder then them</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kinladar</b> on <b>February 09, 2005, 01:48:12 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">The only thing that makes FR hard, is the AE Rampage, and AoE spell he casts.<br /><br />The Rampage is easily avoided by staying at max range, using wolf form for a lower impact point, (don&#039;t ask my why it matters, but in parses I saw it to be true) and don&#039;t use levitation. You&#039;ll rarely get nailed with the AE rampage at least, and then use a timing pattern for the AoE spell. You clerics can heal outside of the AoE range, so as long as they have deep mana pools, all AA mana regen stuff stacked up, I see no reason they couldn&#039;t.<br /><br />FR is really gimp melee DPS compared to some GoD and OoW stuff. There&#039;s no adds, so a little timing, luck and skill will take him down with two groups.<br /><br />Honestly, I&#039;d prolly just use a few rangers as the primary DPS, they&#039;ll never get hit with the rampage, or AoE that way, all ya gotta do then is keep the tank up.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
