					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Tiiden</b> on <b>February 09, 2005, 06:26:56 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Fennin is a total pussy, I wouldn&#039;t rule out the possibilty that people in mostly anguish / pg raid loot could ONE group him.&nbsp; Clerics at that level of the game can chain CHs for a VERY long time.&nbsp; In fact, on a horse with enough regen buffs they could perhaps do it indefinitely.&nbsp; I&#039;d take a cleric, a warrior, a shaman and three rogues.&nbsp; The AE is -700 fire check, but at max spell shield it would only be hitting for 1950, every 60 seconds according to lucy data, plus the 100 pt/tick dot.&nbsp; That&#039;s only 32 damage per second from the DD, or 292 per tick with the dot included.&nbsp; Serenity is 820 per tick heal, which a shaman at that gear level could easily keep up on three rogues indefinitely.<br /><br />Max hit on a warrior is 1962, with 35% shielding that&#039;s 1275, or a max round of 5101 non-disc, 2806 with disc.&nbsp; So under defensive disc, an anguish warrior (assuming over 17k buffed) could sustain 6 FULL combat rounds.&nbsp; If fennin is hitting at the standard mob attack delay (30) then ONE cleric could keep the tank up while under disc, two while not, simply chaining CHs, with ZERO chance of the tank dying.&nbsp; The chance of the tank eating three full combat rounds in a row is statistically impossible.&nbsp; With a shaman patch healing, I feel confident that one cleric could keep the tank up vs an unslowed fennin (I don&#039;t know if he&#039;s slowable at all...), even when riposets are taken into account (assuming warrior is using epic 2 and dented battleworn aegis).&nbsp; <br /><br />I hope Tidil doesn&#039;t read this, or he&#039;ll fall into a nerd induced coma...</div>
					<br />
