					Post by: <b>Self Destruction</b> on <b>February 14, 2005, 11:43:58 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">(http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v425/Undead13/Xegonydead.jpg)<br /><br />Fun, long fight. I don&#039;t really think IL will have any difficulty with Xeg. The encounter is not overly difficult with a balanced raid. It&#039;s just one of those things where one person not paying attention or doing something they shouldn&#039;t can wipe you quick. Of course, we had very competent leaders and I think that&#039;s why it seemed like it wasn&#039;t that hard. Everyone did a fantastic job.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Tiiden</b> on <b>February 15, 2005, 02:14:32 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">With level 70 and omens gear increasing the baseline for character power up quite a bit, I bet both UoP and IL (and Brew Masters soon enough) will have little trouble beating Xegony and Corinav, as they both are just finding out where to put people to deal with what adds when as most PoP encounters are.&nbsp; <br /><br />Rathe will determine which guild is really the stronger, as it not only requires sheer numbers to beat, but the strategy is much more complex, the fight much more painstaking, and there must be a much greater deal of precision and cooperation from the entire raid force.&nbsp; <br /><br />Rathe has broken guilds before, and though I doubt it will have the effect it once did at level 65, it could still prove troublesome.&nbsp; May the best guild win!&nbsp; :)<br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Self Destruction</b> on <b>February 15, 2005, 03:06:45 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">IL and UoP will both beat the Rathe.&nbsp; :cwm20:</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>salben</b> on <b>February 15, 2005, 03:42:40 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I disagree totally, between rathe and coirnav, coirnav requires more numbers then rathe does. Rathe is a strategy fight no doubt, cooperation and teamwork is a must for rathe.<br /><br />Coirnav is a PURE dps fight, it almost comes down to zerging depending on how you look at it. Coirnav requires the higher number to get the proper dps out to beat the timer. Rathe just requires patience and teamwork/strategy more so then having numbers online.<br /><br />I have seen a guild beat rathe with 48 people, but run out of time on coirnav with 68 people the next week. ( and yes they have beat both encounters before). I agree the rathe will be a test for both IL and UoP, I have no doubt that both guilds will pass it with ease after a few attempts.<br /><br />I just see coirnav being the bigger bottleneck here, with the decrease in numbers for almost all guilds, it will be hard to muster that kind of dps for such a intensely dps required fight.<br /><br />edit: I can&#039;t type for crap! I had to edit my edit for a typo!<br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Tiiden</b> on <b>February 15, 2005, 05:35:20 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Eh, I dunno about that.&nbsp; If we&#039;re talking about elemental level players who&#039;ve never faced rathe before, I think the number requirements are greater for Rathe.&nbsp; Obviously top end tanks and healers would make things vastly easier since one warrior could offtank 2-3 councilmen at once.&nbsp; But at the elemental level of play, you need 5 solid offtanks aside from your MT, and two healers for each offtank group, plus enough to chain on that last councilmen, and then enough dps to kill them all in 7 minutes.&nbsp; Elemental geared rogues have less than half the damage output of tacvi/anguish warriors heh.<br /><br />Corinav is pretty much all about pulling and posistioning.&nbsp; If you can get those two aspects down perfectly, the mobs have shit for hps and I fail to see why a guild couldn&#039;t win with 50ish.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kinladar</b> on <b>February 15, 2005, 07:29:52 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Cornaiv is all about AoE nukes, and burning down the trash while controlling the nameds that spawn. Controlling the named can be a tricky thing, but pulling is by far the more critical thing and killing them quickly. <br /><br />Rathe I would also consider a bit easier, because as stated, it&#039;s more about patience, and such, and in a way endurance, rather than DPS. Pulling still critical there as well.<br /><br />But as someone stated, level 70, and the OoW attunable gear, and other odd things, along with spells such as Conviction, and better mana buffs, do make these encounters easier, but there still needs to be a certain skill level and coordination to accomplish them.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Moraganna</b> on <b>February 15, 2005, 08:36:34 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I think it is more how much the players stop the chatter and pay attention to what is going on with all raid encounters. If everyone can stay focused and not take a long time getting started is key. When you sit around for hours and hours just waiting to start people loose interest and do not pay attention as well. </div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Shakro</b> on <b>February 15, 2005, 10:19:52 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">It&#039;s really a class issue, imo.&nbsp; If you&#039;re short on AE nuke classes, especially wizards, you&#039;re going to struggle with Coirnav&#039;s timer.&nbsp; If you&#039;re short on chanters and/or tanks, you&#039;ll have trouble with TRC.&nbsp; I think both will require close to full raids, even now, due to the way the encounters are structured.&nbsp; I suspect that the guilds who are currently progressing (grats to UoP and IL on their recent kills!) might need to recruit a little more or join forces to get those done quickly.&nbsp; Unless level 70 has changed the dynamics more than I&#039;m thinking.&nbsp; </div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Spaerhawk</b> on <b>February 15, 2005, 10:46:33 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I must say, Xegony was by far the most fun I&#039;ve had raid-encounter wise. What a fight it is, lol. I really had to be on my game as a Paladin - RGC / CT&#039;ing, rez&#039;ing, group healing, spot healing, LoH&#039;ing, off-tanking - what a fight!<br /><br />I&#039;m disappointed, though, that I didn&#039;t get a SS of the rainbow. Lol.<br /><br />Cheers.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Callon</b> on <b>February 15, 2005, 11:27:20 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">I just see coirnav being the bigger bottleneck here, with the decrease in numbers for almost all guilds, it will be hard to muster that kind of dps for such a intensely dps required fight.</div><br /><br />UoP had a full raid last night.&nbsp; We booted a couple boxed characters out of the raid to make room for more mains.&nbsp; <br /><br />Xegony was a fun fight.&nbsp; All the wave mobs still have the screwiest bounce around some no matter what the tank does aggro... it&#039;s annoying, but doable.&nbsp; &nbsp; <br /><br />Pulling on Coirnav is pretty solid so far.&nbsp; But the 3 named.... bleh.&nbsp; Still, we should have that encounter figured out soon.&nbsp; Tanks for the rathe council are certainly easier to get than they were without L70s.&nbsp; We have a number of backup tanks with 11k to 12k hit points buffed out, which will be plenty and is probably more than the main tanks had for the first wave of guilds breaking into Time (plus L70 vs. L65).&nbsp; WTB enchanters.<br /><br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Prodigy</b> on <b>February 15, 2005, 12:00:12 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I find it funny that I see a lot of gratz and talk about IL and UoP and just recently BM.&nbsp; When DN is in the same place, and was in ele before BM.&nbsp; We do not raid as often as IL and UoP and did not use &quot;outside&quot; help to boost us up, and yet no talk about DN.<br /><br />We basically have brought people who are totally new to raiding, molded them into fine players, they Did not have OoW gear, spells, etc.&nbsp; but are getting them as we go along and have beaten encounters with far less people than other guilds.&nbsp; <br /><br />Bring the well new expansions, new gear yadda yadda yadda make the encounters less challenging, well that holds true if those people have those gear, spells, which a majority of our people do not. <br /><br />I do admit that the events are less challenging, having been through them multiple times I know how each one works.&nbsp; Problem which some guilds have and reason it takes a while to beat them is improper leadership, and inexperience, not gear.&nbsp; Gear just allows more mistakes with less consequences.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Callon</b> on <b>February 15, 2005, 01:02:07 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I can&#039;t resist... Prodigy&#039;s firing up the drama!&nbsp;  8)<br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">I find it funny that I see a lot of gratz and talk about IL and UoP and just recently BM.&nbsp; When DN is in the same place, and was in ele before BM.&nbsp; We do not raid as often as IL and UoP and did not use &quot;outside&quot; help to boost us up, and yet no talk about DN.</div><br /><br />So IL and UoP get their kills thanks to outside help?&nbsp; How would you know that?&nbsp; I can&#039;t speak for IL, but in UoP&#039;s case you&#039;re very wrong.&nbsp; We&#039;ll have a couple guests here and there on some raids, but the raid force is almost entirely UoP members.&nbsp; Period.<br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">We basically have brought people who are totally new to raiding, molded them into fine players, they Did not have OoW gear, spells, etc.&nbsp; but are getting them as we go along and have beaten encounters with far less people than other guilds.&nbsp; </div><br /><br />You&#039;re late to the party.&nbsp; We already had the &quot;our guild is better because we&#039;re currently killing Blazzax the Omnifiend! with X number of people&quot; rants last week.&nbsp; Get with it!&nbsp;  :cwm20:&nbsp; But the &quot;our players are bigger newbs than your players&quot; claim is a new one, at least lately.&nbsp; I&#039;ll have to remember that one.&nbsp; <br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">Bring the well new expansions, new gear yadda yadda yadda make the encounters less challenging, well that holds true if those people have those gear, spells, which a majority of our people do not. </div><br /><br />And they&#039;re not over L65 and haven&#039;t gained anything significant from GoD/OoW even in single groups?&nbsp; I find that very hard to believe.&nbsp; Not that old encounters being less challenging as a result matters for the top ten list.&nbsp; It&#039;s just a current listing of how far each guild has advanced.&nbsp; <br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">I do admit that the events are less challenging, having been through them multiple times I know how each one works.&nbsp; Problem which some guilds have and reason it takes a while to beat them is improper leadership, and inexperience, not gear.&nbsp; Gear just allows more mistakes with less consequences.</div><br /><br />Of course.&nbsp; We benefit by having a bigger margin of error than those who did these raids first had.&nbsp; For guilds with a lot more fairly casual players than the hardcore raid guilds, that&#039;s good.&nbsp; <br />&nbsp; </div>
					<br />
