					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Prodigy</b> on <b>February 15, 2005, 02:01:15 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="codeheader">Code:</div><div class="code"></div>So IL and UoP get their kills thanks to outside help?&nbsp; How would you know that?&nbsp; I can&#039;t speak for IL, but in UoP&#039;s case you&#039;re very wrong.&nbsp; We&#039;ll have a couple guests here and there on some raids, but the raid force is almost entirely UoP members.&nbsp; Period.<div class="codeheader">Code:</div><div class="code"></div><br />I&#039;m sure people new exactly who I was refering to when I said &quot;outside help&quot;<br /><br /><br /><div class="codeheader">Code:</div><div class="code"></div>You&#039;re late to the party.&nbsp; We already had the &quot;our guild is better because we&#039;re currently killing Blazzax the Omnifiend! with X number of people&quot; rants last week.&nbsp; Get with it!&nbsp; &nbsp;  But the &quot;our players are bigger newbs than your players&quot; claim is a new one, at least lately.&nbsp; I&#039;ll have to remember that one. <div class="codeheader">Code:</div><div class="code"></div><br />Well this is my opinion only.&nbsp; A guild who takes several attempts to kill x mob and continues to fail for a couple monthes and another guild comes in and does it only on their 2nd attempt under the same conditions and with less people is a far better guild than the guild who continues to fail.&nbsp; Top Ten List in no way reflects how good your guild is.&nbsp; Just like you said.&nbsp; How far are they in progression.&nbsp; The only reason I am not going into details with either statement is because I am trying to keep good relations. <br /><br />DN is new.&nbsp; UoP has been around for a while.&nbsp; BM has been around for a while.&nbsp; IL has been raiding a few monthes before DN has.This is in no way a flame inc.&nbsp; If you look at the rate of progression from all guilds.&nbsp; DN, IL would be ahead of UoP and BM, I feel we are a better guild.&nbsp; We are progressing rather quickly even though the amount of time we raid does not compare with IL or UoP.<br /><br />Say what you want about well until you kill FR and Xegony you can&#039;t claim to be as good as us, but we all know FR isn&#039;t much to fall over about and neither is Xegony.<br />And considering the amount of time you have spent in elementals, I would have expected a Xegony kill a lot sooner.<br /><br />All goes back to rate of progression.&nbsp; From DN (november was first recruiting only had maybe 14 people) forming as a non raiding casual guild, then morphing into a 3 day raiding guild then recruiting, building, people who are new to raiding, coming from family guilds.&nbsp; Little aa&#039;s hardly if any oow, GoD (still getting players&nbsp; to even purchase that expansion :) !) farming, and molding them into raiding players.&nbsp; Then taking these &quot;new raiding&quot; people, and accomplishing what we have in the couple of monthes has something to be said.&nbsp; /hats off to the members of DN, and applicants.&nbsp; in no way shape or form did i say they were newbs.&nbsp; They are the complete opposite.&nbsp; They are they people with no ego trip, humble, wanting to be lead, wanting to learn players whom are a guild&#039;s dream.&nbsp; <br />They are able to adapt to unknown variables that are thrown into raids.&nbsp; They listen attentively, when they are given a job, they do it to the best of their ability, they DO NOT whine, and they learn fast.<br /><br />That what it takes to be a great raiding force.&nbsp; <br /><br />So my previous post was not a flame to anyone. Sorry you took it that way, yet i&#039;m not suprised for the retaliation.&nbsp; DN has earned their notched and deserves to be noted, that was the primary point to my previous post.<br /><br /> 8)</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
