					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Rednight $txt[176] February 15, 2005, 03:41:45 pm</div><div class="quote"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Prodigy $txt[176] February 15, 2005, 03:26:20 pm</div><div class="quote">When you have people from a high end guild having key roles in your raid.&nbsp; Such as either being MT, Main CC, main Healer, and leaving YOUR guild just as dps.&nbsp; You don&#039;t deserve that flag.&nbsp; You basically have leaced it, imo.&nbsp; <br /></div><br /><br />Thats funny, you call yer group a bunch of newbies but yet half yer guild is ex-Conviction.&nbsp; All sporting GoD/Time equip/skill level....<br /><br /></div><br /><br />It&#039;s not nessecarily that so many of them are ex-conviction (Prodigy is actually Kinadorm, whom Conviction did gear up to some degree, but the character changed hands more than once and I believe was server transferred and geared out in another guild, since I know we didn&#039;t get him a darkblade) but that they like to actively try and poach our apps, or anyone interested in Conviction - or perhaps other guilds as well.<br /><br />For awhile, due to lack of control over our old website, Ferniss (who used to be Conviction&#039;s application officer under the &quot;old regime&quot;) was still recieving all of our applications in his email, and actively attempting to steal them away.&nbsp; When we finially fixed that, he continued browsing our boards looking for apps posting &quot;Hello&quot; threads in the open section and then trying to recruit them.&nbsp; I&#039;m currently going through and IP banning all DN members from our boards, but I&#039;m sure he will find more creative ways to try and poach our applicants.<br /><br />So they generally get any apps we cut, and some simply heed whatever words he speaks about us and apply to DN instead.&nbsp; I&#039;d be interested to know what the average DN members have been told about the leadership of Conviction... <br /><br />Thought everyone might be interested to know that little piece of history :)</div>
