					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Rylden</b> on <b>February 17, 2005, 11:06:37 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">An open letter to the few morons in this thread who feel it necessary to give their puerile opinions of absolutely no merit.<br /><br />My favorite part about picking sour grapes is the whine that it creates.  Unfortunately, it would appear some people on this board are being just a little over-indulgent.  This sort of self-embarrassment, or martyr syndrome, is generally brought on by not being able to admit they have a problem - namely - they want so badly to be a part of the popular cliques at school, that they rent cheerleaders for prom and purchase workout books that are advertised in the back of comic books.<br /><br />But never fear, true believers, there is hope!  You see, all you need is a dose of reality (tm).  Now, I&#039;m sure this may make your little tummy get all knotty and wired, but I assure you, sometimes taking it all in at once is good for you.<br /><br />Let me give you a few ideas on how you can become a real boy, instead of the groveling, sniveling, little peon you are making yourself, so apparently, out to be.<br /><br />First, proper sentence structure and a tenative grasp of the English language will generally allow you to be looked upon as slightly more than a slug.  People enjoy well-thought out posts, instead of the inane drivel that seems to ooze from your every pore.  Never underestimate the power of an education beyond the third grade.<br /><br />Second, soap and water are things that have been around for centuries.  I know you&#039;ve heard some terrible things about them, particularly what involves drenching yourself in dihydrogen monoxide, but your cares will be washed away!  Soon, you will cause flowers to wilt and dogs to vomit <b>less often</b> because the stench you exude will be tolerable.<br /><br />Lastly, try socializing in more open areas, such as, your living room or the men&#039;s bathroom at Sears.  See, when you&#039;re not sitting in front of your computer all day long awaiting to pounce on your next e-victim, something miraculous occurs!  That&#039;s right, you actually achieve a clue.  And not just any run-of-the-mill clue, mind you, but an honest-to-goodness &quot;Oh what a fucking retard I am&quot; type of clue.  The resulting interactions in public places can help you escape the doldrums of typing one-handed while listening to the latest mix of your three favorite porn videos.<br /><br />Now, you should go right out there and try this.  That&#039;s right... don&#039;t hold back... just give it all your gusto, get the hell off that chair and actually attempt to appear homosapien for a change.  Not only will you impress the few friends you have left, like Bob the Alley Alcoholic and the DnD Geek down the street that only plays drow rangers with variations on the name of Drizzt, but you may actually become a full-fledged member of this thing we call society.<br /><br />Good luck in your endevors, and I hope you make a full recovery from that awful hand lotion &amp; power supply accident swiftly.</div>
					<br />
