					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">If wow and eq2 hadnt come about, I dont know if those same people that quit, wouldnt have just left for some other reason. I guess thats possible as well. I think they were just ready to go.<br />Fact is, with content the way it is now, instancing took a lot of the competition out of the game. Some like it, some dont. We&#039;re #2 now, we&#039;re comfortable there. We were also comfortable at the #3, and #4 spots /shrug<br />As long as my guild is having fun each night together thats all that really counts when it comes down to it.<br />I do think what Gilspur said is quite valid though... WoW and EQ2 didnt just hit those three guilds, they hit everyone.<br />Hege and Ruination bit the dust as well. EiE/DA and Conviction took extremely hard hits. Many old players including long standing officers left from those three guilds too.<br />The difference is...<br />Somehow, for whatever reason, whether it be passion for the game, tenacity or just dumb luck, we were all able to rebuild, reinforce and stick it out.<br />I honestly felt sorry for those that were left &quot;homeless&quot; after WoW and EQ2 hit.<br />But what remains is a less crowded server, lots of instanced content to have fun in, and more good times to come I hope  :approve:</div>
