					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Karshak</b> on <b>February 23, 2005, 09:12:36 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Laylina $txt[176] February 23, 2005, 08:58:10 am</div><div class="quote">Conviction, honestly Im ashamed that I wore your tag when I see some of the posts here by your officers and members.  I thought you had more class than that.<br /></div><br />Why does everything have to be so extreme? Sure, things have gone too far but in the absence of the original posters (props to Prodigy for not disappearing and trying to smooth things over) there was not much else to do but dramatize.<br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Laylina $txt[176] February 23, 2005, 08:58:10 am</div><div class="quote">That was the one thing that the &quot;older Conviction&quot; players did seem to manage well, staying out of most of the RN drama. <br /></div><br />It&#039;s easy to stay out of the RN drama by ignoring it but that doesn&#039;t mean it&#039;s the right thing to do. Remember, an ostrich doesn&#039;t disappear when it sticks it&#039;s head in the sand, it just thinks it does. :) The posts from us have gone too far however because now are are looking like the bad guys here. This wasn&#039;t started by Conviction but we need to end it.<br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Laylina $txt[176] February 23, 2005, 08:58:10 am</div><div class="quote">It didnt take 20 or so posts by you guys to make Plinko look any more of a douche for anon posting a bunch of crap.  So let it go already, you all look like the class bullies.<br /></div><br />True, none were needed but hey, people need to vent. It was annoying to see someone post inflammatory comments from behind an anonymous account. It was even more annoying for them to then disappear once &quot;unmasked&quot;. This probably would have calmed down a whole lot sooner if one of two things hadn&#039;t occurred:<br /><br />1) Plinko or Fernis had come and actually posted.<br />2) It hadn&#039;t been fuel for a few other people to air angst against Conviction.<br /><br />/shrug<br /><br /><br /><br />edit: by the way Laylina, this<div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Laylina $txt[176] February 23, 2005, 08:58:10 am</div><div class="quote">Im not even going to get into the whole pevis waving stuff, because most of the accomplishments that are posted here are honestly not even worth a second glance.<br /></div><br />is as classless as you make Conviction out to be..... Simply because you are at the cutting edge of content makes you no better than people in guilds far behind you in progression terms. I am all for listening to people and looking for the good in a post but to see someone patronize others lack of class then portray elitism that wasn&#039;t earned is annoying too. Oh don&#039;t get me wrong, I am sure you earned it with your hard work and in game excellence, but were you the First Kill specialist of RN or did you move up content by moving up guilds? The accomplishments posted here ARE worth a second glance to those that raided on them, and they have just as much right to be happy about them as you do while you bask in your leetness.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Woodsie</b> on <b>February 23, 2005, 09:42:07 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I was not a member of Conviction under the earlier officers, when I app&#039;ed and came aboard most of the current leaders were leaders then if not in fact but in practice, so I have no comment regarding the previous officers/leaders abilities or lack of abilities. <br /><br />What I do know is me and a lot of others came from a guild where we outfitted the officers and leaders with epics, when we couldn&#039;t get help on our own, who promptly &quot;gave up&quot; on the guild when they were needed most. I for one will always have some bad feelings towards those who seem to use a guild for their own means.&nbsp; Of course in a way we all &quot;use&quot; our guilds, for gear, groups, and etc, but for a lot of us this &quot;using&quot; is no more &quot;using&quot; than how one ueses their own family/friends for support, love, friendship, and etc.<br /><br />To those who have disparaged Convictions accomplishments because they weren&#039;t &quot;firsts&quot;, yes having some clue as to tactics or what to expext sure does help, BUT there is a HUGE difference between reading about something and experiencing it! I do know our first attempt at Uqua final battle the information we had was completly incorrect, either the encounter had been changed or the information we had was incorrect.&nbsp; Conviction learns by doing a lot more than we learn by reading, as most of us don&#039;t read much &lt;g&gt; New app&#039;s from other guilds always seem to comment that we do things different than other guilds, and we do, and damnit we do a damn good job of it.<br /><br />Our current leadership, from our esteemed guild leader to our class leaders deserve a shitload of credit for sticking with it, holding us all together, driving us to do things better/faster, maintaining and building good releationships with most guilds on the server, and for being their day in and day out.&nbsp; BUT, all the credit for the accomplishments does not solely belong with them, it also very much belongs with all the members who log on regularly and give us the ability to raid and beat encounters. Members who put Conviction first, and raid every night even though they know they aren&#039;t going to see an upgrade drop, and maybe have done the raid every week for the past year.<br /><br />So I also applaud the leaders and members of the other guilds in this top ten list, as you guys are still here and for the most part still progressing and doing so in an honorable fashion.&nbsp; For the ones who do so in a less honorable fashion then remember if the core is rotten eventually everything will crumble into slime.<br /><br />My thoughts and views are my own, take them for what they are worth.<br /><br />Woodsie</div>
					<br />
