					Post by: <b>Zorlo</b> on <b>February 23, 2005, 04:43:24 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I read this stupid thread, and the only post that makes any sense was Chubz&#039;s. I&#039;m not in Conv, so i can&#039;t speak on their progress, however, it doesnt seem like they progressed at an insane pace. While they certainly kept dropping targets after their leadership change-up, it wasn&#039;t like the new management did a massively better job as Rylden says. <br /><br />Call me crazy, but perhaps, level 70, new aas, new spells, new recruits, and strats from EiE/DA led as much to their success as any new leadership could have. However, maybe Rylden&#039;s divine mandate to rule an EQ guild inspired people to perform better then they usually can.<br /><br />While i won&#039;t debate the importance of a GL and officers, they are good to have for organization,&nbsp; they arent what &quot;makes&quot; a raid successful. You can have the best EQ &quot;leaders&quot; in the world in your guild, but if the people in it suck at playing, leadership wont inspire them to play better. To be perfectly honest, skill in this game involves clicking a button when you are supposed to, to make sure the blinking colored lights blink in a way that is favorable. Leaders are good to have, but they don&#039;t make or break a guild as you would imply.<br /><br />That being said, I don&#039;t understand why Rylden would claim that, the &quot;new conviction&quot; and especially its &quot;new officers&quot; managed to carry the guild to success they&#039;ve yet to know. No matter what you say or think, you are still building on the time conv spent in the planes, the time that diss spent leading the guild. <br /><br />I don&#039;t think it is too difficult then, at least out of respect for the people that help facilitate your path to where you are now, to show the slightest respect for those before you. If you don&#039;t like diss or w/e, keep it to yourself, or flame him personally, don&#039;t attack his reputation as a GL. Because, no matter what you tell yourself, the new levels help Conviction millions of times more then you help Conviction. <br /><br />Still, that isn&#039;t the point. Officers, like i said, are helpful, but in the end, it is the members that carry a guild, and provide the ability to progress. Perhaps Conviction has improved its rate of progression, but there is no reason to discount their previous achievements, just because you werent directly attached to them.&nbsp; <br /><br /><br /></div>
					<br />
