					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Uqua wasn&#039;t bad, once everyone showed up. <br /><br />That was a piss poor part of Uqua design, you needed alot of tanks, and clerics. The rest was pretty academic.<br /><br />Although, I think at the time we might have been the only guild to use a BDA/WS Ranger to position the Twins at that stage, and not have both Rangers die, I&#039;ll always give the FoT tanks alot of credit, I rarely died on a WS with those guys, White, and kaidog will always go down as two of the best tanks I worked with. Also having some of the best paladins on the server helped. Bobo, Zeno, Sys, and Valcare. <br /><br />Often it wound up being we waited on either tanks to login, or clerics, but rarely both.<br /><br />But we&#039;d have never beaten Uqua without everyone working together, and paying attention, everyone did thier parts, and that is what counted.<br /><br />Had the new games never came out, I could see us making it to Tacvi. Even when just the beta phases started, we lost some key players to EQ2 beta, and WoW beta. <br /><br />But hey, people gotta do what they gotta do, no regrets.</div>
