					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Justyse</b> on <b>March 07, 2005, 04:18:24 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">again, not saying its right... but simply put..<br />because its easier.<br />You can gear someone up quick, get them weapons, flags etc. But teaching raid experience is another thing. They simply might not have the time or desire to do so.<br /><br />Personally we&#039;ve had a lot of luck with people that have left small family guilds/casual guilds for the higher end, and although I dont like to see family guilds suffer because of it, I&#039;m not going to turn someone away if they have the qualities we are looking for.<br />Personality&gt;playtime availability&gt;flags&gt;gear&gt;experience&gt;aa&#039;s<br />We can get new members flags, tons of gear, teach them the ropes, and grind them the aa&#039;s, but what we cant do is make them fun to be around or play when we need them to.<br />I&#039;ll take a n00b with a great personality that plays all damn night long but can LEARN, over a well geared dickhead that has every flag anyday.<br />Now that might keep us #2 forever, but so be it  :cwm9:</div>
					<br />
