					Post by: <b>Kinladar</b> on <b>March 07, 2005, 04:52:44 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Right wrong or somewhere in between, the facts are you will never stop guild poaching, so you may as well accept that you can&#039;t stop it, and simply worry about yourselves.<br /><br />I will state one thing about what you said though Slayyer, I know there are some really good people in EiE, but as someone who has led a guild, you also have to place a certain amount of trust in your officers, and hope that they do not do things you would rather they didn&#039;t. <br /><br />There were a couple times I had to ask FoT officers to knock stuff off, usually after it was to late to prevent a small problem here or there. They are only doing what they think is right to help the guild. It&#039;s not normally done with malice, or to deliberately tear up another guild.<br /><br />It&#039;s not nearly as prevailant as it used to be though, when cockblocks allowed top end guilds to dangle another carrot besides just jumping to the front of content, but also the fact that progression could only occur if that guild allowed it. Or if you apped to them.<br /><br />That is one thing that Instancing took away from many guild who held events such as Rallos Zek, and Emp hostage to keep the other guys out.</div>
