					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Callon</b> on <b>March 09, 2005, 03:27:24 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Zorach, if you want a time+ guild you&#039;re limited to DA/EiE, Conviction, and RoS (in that order).  RoS is doing Uqua.  The other 2 are somewhere beyond that.  Then next three are UoP, DN, and IL.  They&#039;re all making progress now, but none are in Time yet.  If you want an Ascent style guild in terms of very frequent raiding, I think you&#039;d have to go with DA/EiE or Conviction.  RoS raids 3 nights a week and I think #4 thru 6 are all around 3-4 times a week.<br /><br /> </div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>simplee</b> on <b>March 09, 2005, 03:30:06 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Zorach $txt[176] March 09, 2005, 01:39:54 pm</div><div class="quote">So, can I get a current rundown of the top 5? I&#039;m thinkin of coming back on the 16th and kinda wanna see what&#039;s available to choose from.  Being gone 3 months I have no clue where the action is....I just know I am no longer a member of Ascent   :missyou:<br /></div><br /><br />Top 10 Progression (Furthest in Content)<br /><br />1. EiE/DA - Finished with Time, farming upper GoD and Anguish I believe, as well as random OoW mobs.<br />2. Conviction - Farming Time once a week, Farming Qvic, working on Inktuta (almost beat), farming random OoW mobs.<br />3. RoS - Farming Time, random OoW mobs, beat Ikkinz4, working on Uqua<br />4. UoP - farming Elementals, almost to Time (just need Rathe I believe), random OoW mobs<br />5. IL - considered more of a late night/PST guild - working in elemental planes.<br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Spaerhawk</b> on <b>March 09, 2005, 04:07:04 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Are we still agreeing that Time access (i.e. EP God kills) are greater in advancement &quot;points&quot; than stuff in GoD and OoW? I ask because of the grey area between UoP and IL.<br /><br />I&#039;d put the top 5 like this:<br /><br />1. DA / EiE<br />2. Conviction<br />3. RoS<br />4. IL - FR and Xeg down. Ikkinz 1 down, if not Ikk 2. Hulcror (sp?), Feratha, etc.<br />5. UoP - FR, Xeg, Coirnav down. No notable GoD or OoW kills other than random 1.5s.<br /><br />But then again, I was never very knowledgable when it came to raid difficulties that I&#039;ve not done.<br /><br />Cheers.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>xaanru</b> on <b>March 09, 2005, 04:45:46 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Ikkinz would be progression events, so those would count. IMO, Hulcror and Feratha don&#039;t mean much because they are just loot mobs. Nice loot admittedly, but other than some slight gearing up, not really &quot;advancement&quot; per say.<br /><br />So basically, it comes down to: which is more important:<br /><br />Coirnav, or Ikkinz 1 and 2.<br /><br />Again, just an opinion, but the first of those guilds to crack into PoTime, is going to be the first to bust Ikkinz 4 and Uqua, regardless of which has Ikkinz 1 and 2 first, Just because gear matters so much for Uqua, and quite a bit for Ikkinz 4. <br /><br />For that reason alone, I would give the (slight) edge to UoP.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Saltar</b> on <b>March 09, 2005, 04:48:24 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Grats UoP!<br /><br />I knew it would not be long for you to beat the big fish. IMO he is easier than Xeg so when you took her out I figured it was just a matter of Time :). <br /><br />Rathe as we all know is the test for Time but I believe you guys will get it after a round or 2. Rathe is not about strat it is about execution and patience.<br /><br />See you in Time soon!</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Callon</b> on <b>March 09, 2005, 05:12:23 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I&#039;d have to argue that coirnav is much harder than Xeg.&nbsp; Considering how much trouble we had with Coirnav, I think all of UoP would agree.&nbsp; If nothing else, you can restart the Xegony event whenever you want.&nbsp; All you need is a bard.&nbsp; That makes it easy to get multiple attempts a night until you get it right.<br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
