					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Saltar</b> on <b>March 09, 2005, 05:33:57 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I guess it all a matter of opinion. But I know we beat Coirnav with like 57 people. No way you could do Xeg with that many I don&#039;t think.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Redora</b> on <b>March 09, 2005, 05:36:10 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">yeah, I&#039;d have to agree with Callon. With Coirnav your execution has to be right on the money. Any mistakes and you&#039;re screwed. With Xeg...all you really need is a bard and you can reset the event if something goes wrong. Crowd control groups for the adds are pretty easy to set up. Coirnav, you&#039;ve got the 75 trash to kill...then the named to kill...then the charge to coirnav...while keeping all the people you can alive for the final fight....not to mention all the trash respawns when Coir becomes targetable. All that in 14 minutes...ouch. Xeg we took out on second night trying her, coirnav...we were trying to kill him since end of January. hehehe<br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Slayyerr</b> on <b>March 09, 2005, 05:43:43 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I would put Ikk 3 and 4 maybe as true tests for the upcoming UoP, IL, and DN battle for position. Reasoning is that all 4 GoDs can be zerged to an extent. You can throw a ton of people at them and with some coordination get thru the GoDs. Ikk raids minimize the zerg factor somewhat by limiting you  to a set number of raiders (54). Rathe is still a test IMO, you can have 85 peeps in zone, but you still must execute. You have a larger margin of error due to higher numbers on the GoDs. Skill and progression will show more when Ikk 3 and 4 come into play. Plus by looking at the rosters it looks as thou some guilds have gained Upper geared tanks (Time+) that actually allow those guilds to actually get an edge they did not once have at their disposable. You gain benefit from the higher HP that are above the current content your guild is currently doing. So to actually judge where UoP,IL, and DN goes when the gear begins to get closer to actual content and numbers are limited, then we may see some seperation or we may not.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Eaglesky</b> on <b>March 09, 2005, 06:09:17 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Saltar $txt[176] March 09, 2005, 05:33:57 pm</div><div class="quote">I guess it all a matter of opinion. But I know we beat Coirnav with like 57 people. No way you could do Xeg with that many I don&#039;t think.<br /></div><br /><br />Inner Loop took Xegony down with 45 people on their win so yes you can drop Xegony with that many or less.. Coirnav is more DPS than anything Xegony is all about strat and mana regen.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Self Destruction</b> on <b>March 09, 2005, 06:43:56 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Xegony for us was cake. Coir on the other hand was tough as hell. No individual part of the Coir even was super challenging, it was just getting each part to work nearly flawlessly within the time constraints that caused us so many failures. Xegony, I don&#039;t mind, but I don&#039;t care if I ever see Coir again. (although I&#039;ll surely do my best to be there on future attempts)</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
