					Post by: <b>Justyse</b> on <b>March 12, 2005, 09:04:37 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">just a smitten of advice.<br />Dont ignore ikkinz 1 and 2. Even if you arent completely <i>ready</i> for GoD progression yet, you still need them, and the gear netted from a single night in those raids is worth the time. <br />Its also an amazing learning experience.<br />If you notice, this game, and its progression is built in stages. :cwm13: No really? she must be kidding!<br />Prior mobs teach, if you will, a little about the strat needed to kill a higher lvl one.<br />Not in all cases, but in many.<br />Things that happen in Ikkinz 1 &amp; 2 for example are used in later areas of GoD. <br />Its worth the learning experience, and <span style="text-decoration: underline;">definately</span> worth the farming.<br />Its instanced, so no fighting over if a mob is up or if someone else is after it.<br />Doing the same content over and over for progression is so boring, doing something completely different definately helps break up the monotony of having to do &quot;required&quot; targets. <br />Cuz in the end, this is a game, if people get bored... they wont show up. :shrug:</div>
