					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I think people missed the point of my comparison of the Elemental GOD kills to GoD progression. SOE realized that after a point you can &quot;zerg&quot; them in fact without a ton of peeps you can forget attempting the Rathe. So their remedy limit hte raid size to 54 and show me your guild has skill. From my understanding UoP had 80 people in the zone when they dropped Cornav. 56 remained after the minis to throw at him at the end. Did all guild have alot of peeps on first kill, yes but by no means were they all level 70 with new spells and gear. Yes its an old agrument, but it is still considered a *footnote. Like I said before if the 4 guild fighting position want to have a firm grip on where they are, &quot;PROVE&quot; your skill and get into the limited zones and show you can use skills instead of numbers. FR can be 3 grouped. Corniav can be done with 54 i&#039;d say. Xeg has been done with 45 so it seems now. If you want to prove your better then put up or shutup. Get into something that requires some skill and limited numbers, then you can talk rankings. Ikk 1 and 2 are a wash. Ikk 3 and 4 will be a very much step up in tuffness. Phase 1-3 in time are a wash. Get by VZ and TZ in Time and you can say you&#039;ve done something. Heck VZ and Inny are probably the 2 toughest mobs in Time, Quarm is a joke. Stop the babbling get thru the kills then come back and post. OoW sinlge mobs are not a measure of strength. This is to not tarnish UoP&#039;s progression as of late, but get into the new content between the 3 of you (UoP, IL, and DN) then you guys can start the battle. Someone said the Top 3 is what matters atm because of the gap. There is a huge gap between 3 and the others. There is also a huge gap between 3 and 1. Conviction adn RoS are not too far apart, but they have a leg up and can farm the crap out of Qvic with no competition which will pay off immensely in the next little bit. I am sure the next few weeks will definately provide for some good&nbsp; :cwm39:</div>
