					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Zerxes</b> on <b>March 14, 2005, 11:00:55 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Zerxes tells all!<br /><br />First, I&#039;m undecided if that is the Gonaiel that I knew in UoP - the grammar and spelling is a tad better than I remember&nbsp; :)<br /><br />Just a recap on the UoP &quot;exodus&quot;:<br /><br />Zerxes, Sonard, Arweena, Evelyne, Sippi and Xantarre all left at the same time (technically, I was the first, but all 6 of us knew we were going to leave :)).&nbsp; Sippi knew people in RoS and arranged for a &quot;package&quot; deal (they didn&#039;t necessarily need rogues, but 2 clerics and a bard was too much to pass up).<br /><br />Gonaiel apped to RoS at the same time as well as some other UoP, who later withdrew their apps and went back to UoP.<br /><br />After Gonaiel, and in no particular order:&nbsp; Saltar, Slayyerr, Soulmate, Kayela, Delfino, Manntooth, Austin, Kirl, Dauvan, Kerbo . . . that&#039;s only about 17 total, but they were all &quot;core&quot; raiders.&nbsp; I know I&#039;m forgetting some hehe.&nbsp; Also, many people flat out quit around that time because of the problems and lack of leadership due to Mig&#039;s absence.<br /><br />Contrary to Migatol&#039;s posts, UoP did have a policy of &quot;blocking&quot;.&nbsp; I knew about it.&nbsp; We discussed it in the officer forums.&nbsp; If I were to go back in time, however, I would do the same thing.&nbsp; Mobs with 6 day spawns in a non-instanced zone that is basically &quot;Candyland&quot; is poor design on SoE&#039;s part.&nbsp; Its going to foster that kind of behavior.&nbsp; So yeah, I was surprised that Migatol had the balls to make that post on Conviction&#039;s boards denying that UoP &quot;blocked&quot; other guilds.<br /><br />Here&#039;s a juicy tidbit:&nbsp; On the infamous night of the conflict with Hegemony in Ssra, Migatol asked me while talking on the phone to him to intentionally train them.&nbsp; When I told him &quot;No&quot;, he said &quot;Yeah I&#039;m just kidding . . . .&quot;&nbsp; Uh huh.<br /><br />At times, he <b>was</b> in fact busy in tells - he was busy trying to play mediator with the clerics, which was a non-stop source of drama.<br /><br />Migatol actually <b>was</b> a good leader . . . when he was there.&nbsp; I&#039;m not sure when you joined UoP Gonaiel, but he was very active up until around the beginning of the Ssra/VT era for UoP.&nbsp; And quite frankly, he was a fun guy to play the game with.&nbsp; Generally speaking, he had the ability to raise morale, he&#039;s a smart guy, and he was fair.&nbsp; While he was active, he truly had UoP&#039;s best interests at heart (and I know some people won&#039;t believe that, but I honestly believe I knew him better than most people and I&#039;m convinced this was true), unlike some other officers that felt UoP was meant to serve their best interests.&nbsp; With that being said, he was human, like all of us, and he made some bad decisions.&nbsp; One particular being that he was so concerned about hurting a few people&#039;s feelings that he couldn&#039;t make &quot;hard&quot; decisions (e.g., the whole cleric issue).&nbsp; Ironically, he ended up doing just that by not being honest and telling some of the clerics that he wasn&#039;t going to solve the problem due to his fear of hurting one or more cleric&#039;s feelings.<br /><br />I understand Slayyerr&#039;s issues with Migatol, but I can&#039;t figure out why you have so much angst against him and UoP Gonaiel.&nbsp; Is it all because they wouldn&#039;t invite your sister?<br /><br />Alright, back to your regular &quot;Top 10&quot; thread . . . .</div>
					<br />
