					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I didn&#039;t call it a tool either, someone else did. All I wanted to do was kill the sucker and we did. I did not do it alone, I just &quot;helped&quot; initiate he raid and help with the strats at that time. I didn&#039;t even consider it a rogue faction. I forget what they named &quot;us&quot; but if you recall we even got our own little forum and ErP solution to keep the friction down from the people who were not considered &quot;hard core&quot;. <br /><br />Just a side note. UoP is a casual guild and from RN prospective is one of the VERY few remaining guild to have somewha of a long lasting history. That means they have survived alot coflict. They may struggle, but they still &quot;geter done&quot; so props to them for that. DA/EiE and UoP is probably the only 2 still on the list that have been on RN for more than 3 years and they still survive. RoS also does not require attendance, is casual (3 nights a week) and family style type guild. But we still &quot;geter done&quot; as well. So I ill give UoP a hats off for surviving what has been&nbsp; a very rough time for EQ. I remember before I ever joined a guild I would look at Afterlife and Ascent web pages, just to do the oh and ah of what they were doing. They were trailblazers and at one point were the number 1 guild serverwide. But EQ and RN have bothed chaged dramatically since then. Even thou this can be a who&#039;s better than who thread, everyone has to admit, in a sense that was why this was started. Almost like college football, everyone like to say their tea is number 1, but it is hella fun discussing why. I don&#039;t necessarily like drama, but people sometimes stir it up just to sit back and watch the arguements go on. You can make it fun or you can let it get to you and get mad.&nbsp; 8)<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Zerxes $txt[176] March 16, 2005, 01:21:39 pm</div><div class="quote"><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">Our first AHR kill was lead by my rogue faction while he was away at Fainfiare which also lead to a bitter taste in the officers mouth.</div><br /><br />Gosh, here I was an officer at the raid at the time and little did I know I was actually just a part, or &quot;tool&quot; if you will, of Slayerr&#039;s &quot;rogue faction&quot;  :)<br /><br />Good to hear from you Ialin!<br /></div></div>
