					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Dalla</b> on <b>March 17, 2005, 05:36:57 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Slayerr,<br /><br />First of all whatever happens in EiE is between me, my officers and my members - period.  Whatever was said and done was done with the intention of being fair to the members and maintaining the good reputation that EiE and every single member it has had since it&#039;s inception has worked hard on getting and then maintaining.<br /><br />In additon, anything that may be an EiE issue does not overflow to DA and vice versa.  We are one alliance, but we are most deinfitely two separate guilds.  If you want to call out both of us, you better have your facts straight.<br /><br />Thirdly, this game is rarely about skill and more times about gear and play time.  The rich get richer scenario very much applies to the virtual world of Norrath as well.  I will be happy to allow you to tank anything that would be slightly above your current content on an EiE raid, but we do not feel like dropping back 2 years in content just to gear up our twinks for the night.<br /><br />Finally, DA &amp; EiE just beat the 6th MPG trial for full Anguish access after the most recent changes that Sony has made.  The first time we beat all of these trials, they were pretty much a joke for 3 of them and 3 took some practice.  The current setup of the trials makes the orginal ones look like NTOV.  We did this with mostly new and younger members, about 80% new clerics, 60% new tanks, and almost all of our &quot;support&quot; class people being apps or members under 30 days.  I can assure everyone that this was a herculean effort made by well over 70 people from those that were there everday to those that logged on when they could to help gear up everyone else so that we could beat the trials.<br /><br />Now when you can claim that you are responsible or even significantly contribute to an equal vault in progression for your own guild you can come here and make such challenges and you will have the respect of those that read this board daily.  Until then you are just one more person screaming like a child about something that you have no concept.  You are an unarmed man in a battle of wits.<br /><br />Feel free to prove me wrong.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Slayyerr</b> on <b>March 17, 2005, 05:54:58 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Dalla,<br /><br />Well said an I apologize to DA and EiE. It was not meant as a guild as a whole but at those selevt few I mentioned. It was, however mentioned and whether it was handled behind closed doors or not does not need aired here. BUT, what that select few was doing WAS effecting game play for individuals. I have had several named taken from my groups in PG due that select few due to the fact that they were able to warp to the mob instead of fighting to it like we were. Now as for proof, the proof was in a cheat itself. Not by me but by someone in the zone who was using showeq. Example, named shows on track the ranger says. OK its DK in PG. We are at Body and can get there with about 15 mintues of fight. One minute later DK goes off track. I said how the heck. Then I get a tell from someone (unnamed) that showed those select move on showeq from one end of the zone directly to DK. No spell in the game can take an entire group that distance in that length of time, not even CoH. So yes I made an assumption they were warping. Do I know for a fact, not until it went into tells and was kindly told to just go about my business you lost the mob be done with it. So yes, it effected my game play and pissed me off. That was just one instance. From then I would watch those guys pop from MPG zone in around the corner then one minute later be in a trial. Now put 2 and 2 together. Ok they could have had a mage parked there and SoS rogue to the trial, but guess what no mages were in the zone. That erked me. I am sorry for even mentioning DA and EiE as a whole, you guys have worked hard to get where you are. But that select few was ruining some fun and it wasn&#039;t right. OK so let&#039;s call a GM in they&#039;ll take care of it. We all know that is not gonna happen. Again I am sorry, but that is part of the story.</div>
					<br />
