					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Callon</b> on <b>March 29, 2005, 12:44:24 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">We only had 2 officers that ran the guild for months. <br /><br />Guildleader? Well let&#039;s just say he&#039;s been MIA for months. </div><br /><br />So it&#039;s mostly a lack of people willing to lead?  I didn&#039;t think RoS was hurting too badly for overall numbers.  But as the number of hardcore players on EQ continues to shrink, it makes sense that it&#039;s harder to find good raid guild leaders/officers.  You have to be really into the game to be a good high end raid leader.  There&#039;s time involved in and out of the game getting strats down and the stress of leading it.  The vast majority of more casual players simply don&#039;t want to do it.  It&#039;s not fun for most of them.  <br /><br />I don&#039;t know what RoS&#039;s players will do now.  I suspect some will quit EQ because as with any of the big guilds now, some people are only still playing because of their guild.  The rest?  I don&#039;t know if there are enough openings in up and coming guilds for everyone.  I suppose there will be soon as EQ continues to bleed people.  </div>
