					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Zerxes</b> on <b>March 29, 2005, 04:03:57 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Callon $txt[176] March 29, 2005, 12:44:24 pm</div><div class="quote">So it&#039;s mostly a lack of people willing to lead?&nbsp; I didn&#039;t think RoS was hurting too badly for overall numbers.&nbsp; But as the number of hardcore players on EQ continues to shrink, it makes sense that it&#039;s harder to find good raid guild leaders/officers.&nbsp; You have to be really into the game to be a good high end raid leader.&nbsp; There&#039;s time involved in and out of the game getting strats down and the stress of leading it.&nbsp; The vast majority of more casual players simply don&#039;t want to do it.&nbsp; It&#039;s not fun for most of them.&nbsp; <br /></div><br /><br />I don&#039;t think it was an issue of a lack of people willing to lead at all.&nbsp; As I&#039;m sure you know, the guildleader pretty much has the exclusive power to promote members to officers (pretty sure this is a built in game mechanic, and I know it was the case with RoS).&nbsp; With RoS, as Soulmate mentioned, the guild leader has been MIA for roughly 4 months, and other officers haven&#039;t been playing for various reasons.&nbsp; What RoS was left with was basically 2 officers running the show, and they did a fantastic job of it.&nbsp; Nevertheless, its too much work for 2 people and burnot will certainly occur.&nbsp; Even if you try to delegate authority to other members, if they aren&#039;t officially tagged with officer status in game, it just presents problems.&nbsp; They never really are legitimized as leaders.&nbsp; So these 2 officers really couldn&#039;t get additional help by naming other officers (since only the guild leader has that power).<br /><br />As for numbers, it sounded to me like they were hurting a little near the end, probably in part to the uncertainty cause by the problem described above.&nbsp; They certainly weren&#039;t in trouble when I left at the beginning of the year - one of the main reasons I left was, because of my real life schedule, I wasn&#039;t able to log on right when raids started (I live out West), and if you weren&#039;t at our raids when they started, you pretty much had to stand in line and wait for an opening - even with Time&#039;s 72 person cap.&nbsp; I have no clue what caused the dramatic drop off in numbers between January and March, but I certainly was shocked to find out about this.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Shakro</b> on <b>March 29, 2005, 04:24:31 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Seems like petitioning a GM could have been a viable answer.&nbsp; I did that with an alt guild, the original leader was MIA (actually had quit EQ) and I got the GM to put me in as a co-leader (both of us showed up as L in the guild menu) so we could name other officers...&nbsp; but then I don&#039;t know the facts and I&#039;m sure it was way more complicated than just ability to put &quot;O&quot; next to people&#039;s name.&nbsp; Anyway too bad, RoS had alot of nice people.&nbsp; </div>
