					Post by: <b>Kinladar</b> on <b>April 20, 2005, 08:31:15 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I think these kinds of issues that come up in any guild show how closely the members reflect the leaders ideals, and philosophy.<br /><br />There&#039;s always multiple ways to look at things, and none of them are technically right or wrong, just depends on how a person perceives them.<br /><br />I put more value into the efforts of the guild as a whole, and it just bugged me to see a few people take advantage of those efforts, especially now that you can 5 man in the 6th person with the way the 85% rule was changed.<br /><br />Makes it much easier for a small bloc of players to let those who may never see Qvic, to be able to tag along, and gain some of the better armor in game, for a fee. So those few people who are able to take on those situations, with a small group of 2-3 actual players, and some boxed bots, can make a killing selling the molds.<br /><br />In essense profiting from thier guildmate&#039;s efforts to help them get into Qvic. <br /><br />I just personally think that&#039;s a load of bullshit to do to your guildmates. There&#039;s nothing in SoE&#039;s rules that state it&#039;s wrong, but all in all, it&#039;s about showing respect to those who helped you get to where you are. <br /><br />Before things wound down in December of &#039;04, I had access to, and could have boxed all 6 toons needed to take down Msha&#039;s in Qvic. I had alts that coulda used those molds too, but that was not what it was all about for me. It was about helping guildmates get the gear, and we prefered that you only took FoT people along on those romps. <br /><br />We openly encouraged, and in fact required people to ask in guild 2-3 times before they could ask anyone outside of guild if they needed a class, like a bard etc.... Some people were a bit pissed over that one too, they again sometimes felt we had no right to tell them who they could ask along etc etc etc... And we never denied them that right, we just expected them to ask guildmates first. If thier friends were mad, then thier friends should app to our Guild if they want to do those things so badly was my point of view.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Qutsemnie</b> on <b>April 20, 2005, 04:49:12 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Our alliance pretty much uses what justyce wrote~ In fact her post looks like a post i wrote to defend our policy when someone wanted to debate it.&nbsp; I even used the line about how we all got here only with the guilds effort so deciding now that your an independent agent is wrong.&nbsp; I took a more critical tone though when i said its impractical to have a mob sometimes be DKP and sometimes not be DKP.&nbsp; Either we always hit them pointed or we never hit them as an official target at all. Its impractical to sometimes not do a mob on points, but not on tuesdays when an officers there... That will breed rampant jealousy in about 2.5 seconds. In the end I was most concerned about what puts the most qvic loot in our guildees hands after you conclude that it has to be one or the other (pointed or not pointed) to be practical.&nbsp; I used that with a be careful what you wish for tone. <br /><br />In general if any guild moves from a dkp msha to a nondkp msha i think it will hinge upon whether or not they desire mshas to be a raid target ever again.&nbsp; Once it ceases to be a viable raid target then it becomes more practical to say FFA it.<br /><br />Im not an officer and may not speak for them but ive done some thinking about the msha issue it seems to come up for every guild eventually.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kinladar</b> on <b>April 21, 2005, 09:24:13 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I personally felt they needed to make the Msha&#039;s harder, and it would have eliminated much of the debate. Just increasing thier Melee DPS would have solved it in my opinion. Make it so that even under optimal skill levels and gear taken into consideration, it would still take a minimum of 3 groups to kill one, 4-5 for lesser skilled/equipt players. The only reason these were such a contested thing, is they can be single grouped so easily at later levels of gear and skill.</div>
					<br />
