					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>simplee</b> on <b>April 28, 2005, 09:44:48 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Aaric $txt[176] April 28, 2005, 12:15:03 am</div><div class="quote">I would dare not say you&#039;re #1 in progression in DoN though, you just beat us on Yar&#039;Lir run today by 15 minutes.<br /><br />We finally decided to do DoN since the expansion released :P First time we actually hit it as a raid lol.<br /></div><br /><br />I was under the impression that the first guild to a certain point in content was the #1 in progression... did the rules change?  First no longer equals #1 in progression?<br /><br />Both guilds went in there Tuesday night, neither guild won.  We had maybe a handful more then your &quot;scouting crew&quot;, but still far less then the maximum allowed.  <br /><br />Wednesday night was a fun race.  With instanced content, there&#039;s no contest for the actual mob, just who can get it done the fastest.  Who can learn the strats the fastest, move to the zone the fastest, and in some cases who can CR the fastest and get back in there to try again.<br /><br />Be assured, Conviction had people ready for that Tier of progression for quite some time now... but, like DA/EiE, those targets were never a high priority.  I still find it funny that they became priorities for both guilds at the same time.<br /><br />Grats on your perserverance last night.  Loots probably aren&#039;t on par with what you see in Anguish, but still some very nice stuff, and overall, it was a great battle, and a fun fight to figure out.  Not to mention, a damn fine looking dragon model!<br /><br />(PS - it was more then 30 minutes)</div>
