					Post by: <b>Shrek</b> on <b>May 01, 2005, 05:20:44 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I could be wrong here, but reality is based on perception not the truth.&nbsp; The perception is some Conviction members came here bragging that they were #1 in something.<br /><br />There&#039;s nothing wrong with this, since everyone wants to be #1 ...<br /><br />In this case it just comes off as hollow.&nbsp; You beat an encounter, which DA/EiE could probably have done months ago.&nbsp; Why they didn&#039;t I don&#039;t know.&nbsp; But since even your own members shy away from stating they are #1 it just seems.... odd.<br /><br />There&#039;s nothing wrong with being proud of a server first, but to actually state you are #1 in something, when the &quot;competition&quot; is admittedly (by your own people) better than you are.&nbsp; They simply just didn&#039;t enter the race.<br /><br />Maybe the times have changed, people seem a lot less, animated.&nbsp; Back in the day, when DA/EiE was the first to kill the boss in lower acrylia, had I gone to VN and posted some lame duck, we&#039;re #1 in luclin post, I&#039;d have been laughed at by everyone on the server, let alone Ascent.&nbsp; The encounter was not very difficult, and had Ascent put any effort into it they could have done it.<br /><br />Maybe I&#039;m just too old school, but you didn&#039;t say you were #1 unless you really were.&nbsp; A server first, is one thing, being #1 is another.&nbsp; The arguement that we can be #1 in this and you can be #1 in that just doesn&#039;t hold water for me.&nbsp; RN, and EQ in general has had a very distinct meaning behind being #1.<br /><br />If you are not the best, then you are not #1.<br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
