					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Self Destruction</b> on <b>May 03, 2005, 12:00:44 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Givins $txt[176] May 02, 2005, 11:43:00 pm</div><div class="quote"><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">&nbsp; Ya something hapened . as UoP was starting CoH, Two groups of IL set up, pulled trigger, and blew coirnav spaw for 12 hours.<br />Odly enough that put the respawn right in IL&#039;s raid time.</div><br /><br />Between OA and UoP, we couldn&#039;t even get a shot at Coirnav.&nbsp; Both OA and UoP knew damn well that we were waiting on Coirnav to get into Time, and neither guild offerred to let us have a chance at him.&nbsp; If we didn&#039;t do anything, we&#039;d probably be waiting for a month to get into Time.&nbsp; We had to do something.&nbsp; &nbsp; <br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote"> Grats IL ..&nbsp; &nbsp;  you do it with class!!</div><br /><br />As has been mentioned before, it&#039;s well known that UoP is not above such tactics.&nbsp; All that cock blocking that you guys had done in the past came back on you.&nbsp; It&#039;s karma.&nbsp; In fact, I wouldn&#039;t be surprised that the reason IL was unable to get a chance at Coirnav at all was because you guys were doing the same thing to us, and we just didn&#039;t know it.&nbsp; <br /><br />Oh well, I&#039;m just glad that we are out of that little log jam.&nbsp; We were starting to wonder if we&#039;d ever get a chance to kill Coirnav.&nbsp; Hopefully we&#039;ll never have to compete for the same mob ever again.&nbsp; <br /></div><br /><br />We haven&#039;t done a single Time raid yet. The reason for this is that we do not have enough yet flagged to do so. We&#039;ve been trying to catch Coir for a couple weeks now to do him again so we can move forward. UoP needed Coir just as much as IL did.<br /><br />And the UoP I joined and am currently in has not used this type of tactic at any time that I&#039;m aware of (maybe in the past and under different leadership, but whatever). Even still, as far as I know we&#039;ve been nothing but courteous and polite with IL, but then IL blocks on a trigger and suddenly we deserve it? Heh...ok. Just remember that when later on someone may do it to you. Personally though, I&#039;d have rather just not seen this type of thing happen.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Givins</b> on <b>May 03, 2005, 04:10:54 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote">  We&#039;ve been trying to catch Coir for a couple weeks now to do him again so we can move forward. UoP needed Coir just as much as IL did </div><br /><br />Bullshit.  You guys wiped on Coirnav last weekend. You guys have had a zillion chances, and apparently have blown all of them except one.  Coirnav isn&#039;t UoP&#039;s God Given Spawn.  <br /><br />Really the problem has been more that OA has suddenly decided to bypass Arbiter and Xegony and has gone after Coirnav like 5 out of the last 7 spawns.  It really has very little to do with either UoP or IL.  <br /><div class="smalltext">Quote:</div><div class="quote"> you have to fight for kills in this game you cant expect other guilds to step out of your way and give you free attempts at mobs </div><br /><br />That quotation is from a UoP member, right?  Why is it that when other guilds complain about wanting a chance at Coirnav, you guys say crap like that, but when others do fight for a kill, you complain?  Fighting for kills is a 2 way street, UoP.  <br /><br />I want to emphasize that we attempted to play nice and wait out all of yall&#039;s attempts and backflags, but we got sick of waiting, as mostly OA wiped over and over and over.  It became apparent that neither guild was interested in giving us a shot at him.  Our guild has been chomping at the bit to get into Time for many weeks now.  So we took matters into our own hands.  If we hadn&#039;t, who knows how many more OA and UoP wipes we would have had to wait out before Coirnav was left unmolested for IL to attempt?  It would have been another month.  Sorry, we just aren&#039;t interested in waiting that long.  <br /><br />One more little factoid I would like to bring to light:  our officers contacted UoP officers about joining forces to kill Coirnav, but UoP refused.  UoP was also asked to allow IL to allow one of its members to come along on their recent Rathe Council kill, but was refused.  It would have been very simple to trade a few flags between the two guilds.  You guys could have gotten a few Coirnav flags, we could have gotten (one I believe) a flag for Rathe Council.  IL has never been a flag hog.   We have often allowed a few stragglers to come along on our raids just to pick up a flag.  It&#039;s simply not our fault that you guys have members that still need the flag.  It&#039;s UoP&#039;s.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Self Destruction</b> on <b>May 03, 2005, 04:54:53 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Givins $txt[176] May 03, 2005, 04:10:54 am</div><div class="quote">Bullshit.&nbsp; You guys wiped on Coirnav last weekend. You guys have had a zillion chances, and apparently have blown all of them except one.&nbsp; Coirnav isn&#039;t UoP&#039;s God Given Spawn.<br /></div><br /><br />Wow, you&#039;re not even trying to be civil, are you? I don&#039;t understand how you twisted what I said to make it sound like I was saying that Coir was for UoP only. I said nothing of the sort. We weren&#039;t even attempting Coir for some time after our first success. What I said was that UoP has been after Coir for a couple weeks now...as in, we&#039;d like to kill him again so that we can finish our flagging. IL&#039;s chomping at the bit to raid Time? I guess you think we&#039;re still trying to kill Coir because the event is fun?<br /><br />...it&#039;s our <i>fault</i> some members of our semi-casual guild don&#039;t have the Coir flag? If you say so. This is something we were trying to remedy however. And as far as flag sharing goes, that kind of policy is set by the officers. Personally, I don&#039;t see a problem allowing someone from a guild (who has beaten the event they are tagging for) to tag along for a flag, but that&#039;s not up to me. If the officers don&#039;t want to do this either due to the hassle of it or simply because they would prefer we do things on our own, I&#039;m not sure this is even a negative thing. It&#039;s not as though UoP members are being told to go hassle guilds for flags they&#039;re missing, but we won&#039;t let anyone come along in return. Anyway, I can&#039;t speak to the reasons for this as I&#039;m not an officer, nor do I speak for the guild in any way other than just to state my opinion.<br /><br />Also, that comment about waiting for us to wipe a few more times is classy too. You&#039;re some kind of gentlemen&#039;s gentleman. It&#039;s also pretty cool that you&#039;re trying to make us sound like the bad guys, when we&#039;ve done nothing intentionally to harm IL. Meanwhile a couple groups from IL are in fact the ones who killed the trigger to keep other guilds from doing the event. How&#039;s that work?<br /><br />I didn&#039;t have a problem at all with IL and I still don&#039;t. I think you guys are good people including the officers. (that I know of)&nbsp; I just think this one situation was a bit messed up and I&#039;ve tried to express that as civily as possible, but you&#039;ve apparently decided to belittle and degrade UoP and pass this off as everyone else&#039;s fault. Whatever suits you, I guess.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Nartuuk</b> on <b>May 03, 2005, 05:54:27 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">How about we just say grats to IL on the kill, and grats to UoP and OA for now being able to have Coirnav all to themselves! No more fighting for targets from here on out...thats the way it should always be!</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Carsonn</b> on <b>May 03, 2005, 05:57:00 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">UoP leadship has been known to Cock Block on many things.  About Half of your leaders have been a party to that stuff and thats fine  but don&#039;t cry about it when it happens to you.<br /><br />As far as OA is conserned we have only attempted Coirnav 3 times so I have no idea where you get this 5 out of 7 times crap from.  Also who says OA has to do FR then xegony then coirnav then TRC ?  If we want to do TRC first then what ever the hell we want to thats our choice.  There is no rule that says you have to do any flag mob in order for pop progression.  We can kill RZTW first then Mith Marr if we wanted to that doesn&#039;t mean we are going to but we can.  Granted you can&#039;t go to diffrent zones untill you do teir 1 but there is no set way to do things and there isn&#039;t an order in what you have to do.  Don&#039;t get bitter at OA becuase we are trying to do mobs that you want.  Personally you can take this straw I have here and suck it up and stop whining about not getting a chance and be damn happy you finally made it to time.  Lord knows you talked all that crap about being better then UoP only to get smoked by them and DN to time.  </div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
