					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Zerxes</b> on <b>May 03, 2005, 11:43:08 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">&quot;Cock-blocking&quot; in VT is a bad example - numerous guilds did it starting with Ascent.&nbsp; Arirang to FoT.&nbsp; Forsaken did the same to UoP.&nbsp; It was poor design on Sony&#039;s part by making ONE zone (VT) a virtual &quot;candyland&quot; for loot, with the path there going through ONE mob (the Emperor).<br /><br />Mobs/cycles that can be intentionally blown are a little different from flat out beating a guild to a mob, like UoP did to Hegemony with Emperor, even if it is to prevent them from gaining access to ONE, non-instanced candyland zone.<br /><br />I was an officer in UoP at the time this was happening.&nbsp; The &quot;Asian Alliance&quot; was already in VT at the same time as UoP.&nbsp; With Hegemony, it would have been 3 guilds in VT -- that simply is too many guilds for a zone that repops once every 6 days.&nbsp; Getting VT once every 3 weeks is simply unacceptable.&nbsp; I&#039;m sorry, but if I were to go back in time, I would have done the exact same thing to Hegemony -- if you can beat us to Emperor (which, to their credit, they did eventually), then you can have your shot at VT, but we certainly aren&#039;t going to open the door for you and welcome you to the zone with open arms by sitting aside and saying &quot;Sure, go ahead and take the Emperor.&quot;<br /><br />Oh, and the time Hegemony was in VT and was clearing their way to Blob 1 (they didn&#039;t have CoH set up), and UoP came in and CoH&#039;d to DXXT&#039;s tower, Hegemony petitioned the GM who basically told them &quot;sorry, but you guys don&#039;t have CoH set up and UoP is heading to the second floor, so there is no problem&quot; -- that was pure gold.<br /><br />P.S.&nbsp; I hope all you people complaining about this fighting over mobs, racing guilds, etc. are not planning on playing Vanguard -- because Brad McQuaid promises to bring all this crap right back to you!!!&nbsp;  :)</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
