					Title: <b>Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Shakro</b> on <b>May 04, 2005, 02:03:32 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Is it fair to people with the last name Hitler that they&#039;re judged based on that name?&nbsp; Probably not.&nbsp; Is it fair that people are judged based on the color of their skin?&nbsp; Definitely not.&nbsp; Is it fair to judge a guild, including its newer members, by the history of that guild?&nbsp; Maybe.&nbsp; You choose to wear a guild tag and you get the good and the bad of that guild.&nbsp; That&#039;s why it&#039;s so important to play honorably, and for guilds to police their own and make sure their members don&#039;t cheat, KS, train, etc.&nbsp; Because in EQ, when you&#039;re guilded, what you do is held in favor of or against your guid.&nbsp; And people have very long memories.&nbsp; Just because some of the officers are changed or the membership is altered (people always coming and going in any guild) doesn&#039;t mean that guild history, good or bad, is wiped clean.&nbsp; I honestly think that that&#039;s part of the uniqueness of the game, the social interaction and the history.&nbsp; The lack of competition in today&#039;s EQ, due to instancing of content, means that guilds have far fewer chances to interact (race, KS, cockblock, set up rotations, etc.), either for good or bad, than they used to.&nbsp; So there&#039;s really less opportunity for reputations to develop or change than there used to be.<br /><br />I&#039;m still sad TA and JH are gone.&nbsp; Two very cool guilds, and cool people.</div>
					<br />
